\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar in a tight range, interbank rates ease\b0\par\par\uc2 727 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2009\par 11:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, July 2 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets in late trade on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Close       Morning     Previous close\par                        At 0901 GMT At 0350 GMT At 0901 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>       7.7501/02   7.7501/02   7.7500/01\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>   -62/-58     -64/-58     -63/-60\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>    -112/-107   -112/-107   -112/-107\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>     -180/-170   -185/-175   -185/-175\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>   0.0001      0.0001/0.05 0.01/0.05\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>   0.01/0.09   0.04/0.10   0.05/0.08\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=> 0.25/0.35   0.25/0.35   0.25/0.35\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>   0.55/0.65   0.55/0.65   0.55/0.66\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>    0.97/1.07   1.00/1.07   1.00/1.09\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 * For more live quotes of forwards and interbank rates, click on <FWEN>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar held within a narrow range against the U.S. dollar on Thursday, while interbank rates softened after fund injections by the city's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg amid capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 * The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> traded between 7.7500 and 7.7503 on Thursday, ending little changed from late Tuesday trade in Asia.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said there was buying interest in both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the volumes were not huge.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong financial markets were closed on Wednesday for a public holiday.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index <.HSI> closed 1.09 percent lower on Thursday, shedding early gains as the mood the market swung from optimism over upbeat manufacturing data to caution ahead of key U.S. jobs data.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, the HKMA is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar hits 7.75 or 7.85, to keep the band intact.\par \par \uc2 * The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during Asia and New York trading hours on Tuesday, selling a total of HK$5.813 billion ($750 million) for U.S. dollars to stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation and keep it within its trading band.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar has been boosted by strong capital inflows into the territory in recent weeks, partly attracted by initial public offerings.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will lift the aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- to HK$210.359 billion by July 3 when the transactions are settled.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates were mostly softer because of abundant liquidity in the banking system following HKMA injection.\par \par \uc2 The overnight rate reversed Tuesday's rise triggered by banks seeking short-term funds to balance their books at the end of the month and the second-quarter.\par \par \uc2 Overnight Hibor <HIHKDOND=> was fixed at 0.05000 percent on Thursday morning, down from a three-month high of 0.12500 percent on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 One-month Hibor <HIHKD1MD=> fell to 0.10036 percent from Tuesday's 0.10143 percent. Three-month Hibor <HiHKD3MD=> dipped to 0.34643 percent from 0.35893 percent.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong dollar forwards were little with thin activity, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong retail sales in May dropped by 6.2 percent by value from a year earlier, virtually in line with expections but falling more than in April due to a sharp decline in tourist arrivals last month. [ID:nSP212759]\par \par \uc2 * Market participants are looking ahead to U.S. non-farm payroll data due at 1230 GMT, for fresh trading clues.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. economy is expected to have shed 363,000 jobs in June, more than 345,000 lost in May, and the unemployment rate is forecast to have risen to a 26-year high of 9.6 percent from May's 9.4 percent. [ID:nN01511504]\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS\par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo; Editing by Chris Lewis)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090705e5720005q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
