\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar dips, interbank rates decline\b0\par\par\uc2 694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 2009\par 12:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, May 20 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets in late trade on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Close       Midday      Previous Close\par                        At 0908 GMT At 0400 GMT At 0933 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>       7.7522/25   7.7522/23   7.7511/12\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>   -81/-77     -82/-78     -73/-70\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>    -123/-117   -131/-124   -115/-110\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>     -180/-173   -191/-179   -167/-152\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>   0.00001     0.00001     0.00005\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>   0.01/0.02   0.01/0.02   0.01/0.02\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=> 0.10/0.20   0.15/0.25   0.20/0.30\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>   0.50/0.60   0.50/0.60   0.50/0.68\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>    0.91/1.01   0.94/1.04   1.04/1.14\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 * For more live quotes for forwards and interbank rates, click on <FWEN>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar was marginally lower against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday after rangebound trade, while interbank rates fell further amid abundant liquidity in the banking system and following a decline in Libor rates.\par \par \uc2 A recent drop in interbank rates, which has pushed three-month rates to a four-year low, prompted banking giant \uc2 HSBC\uc2  to cut its deposit rates, effective on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 * Dealers said there was little reaction to Tuesday's news that Joseph Yam would step down as head of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) on October 1 after 16 years. [ID:nHKG255510]\par \par \uc2 "I don't think there will be any impact from his retirement. I personally think that the peg will stay until the Chinese yuan is fully convertible," one dealer said.\par \par \uc2 The government on Tuesday said Yam's retirement would not affect monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar <HKD=> fell 0.02 percent on Wednesday but closed off a session low of 7.7528 against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 One dealer at a foreign bank said there was some real money demand for U.S. dollar, and he expected the spot rate to stay in a range between 7.7500 and 7.7540 in the near term with eyes on developments in the equity market <.HSI>.\par \par \uc2 Another dealer attributed the modest fall to interest rate arbitrage, although arbitrage trades, also known as carry trades, are limited as the interest differential between U.S. and Hong Kong interest rates is very narrow, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Arbitrage trades enable investors to sell Hong Kong dollars for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take advantage of an interest rate differential with the United States.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates plunged on Wednesday, with the three-month Hibor fixing at 0.40571 percent -- its lowest level since January 4, 2005.\par \par \uc2 Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> has dropped 35 basis points since late April, tracking a decline in Libor rates and due to excess liquidity in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the HKMA's frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks which has pushed the aggregate balance to a record high.\par \par \uc2 The overnight Hong Kong interbank rate has remained at near zero.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 HSBC Holdings\uc2  on Wednesday afternoon said it would cut its Hong Kong dollar savings rates by 0.9 basis point to 0.001 percent from 0.01 percent set in March 2008 for deposits of and above HK$5,000.\par \par \uc2 As the rise in the aggregate balance is putting downward pressure on interbank rates, banks are facing growing cost pressures and narrowing interest margins, a spokeswoman for \uc2 HSBC\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 * The discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards widened in the morning amid some selling interest from investment banks but later narrowed as buying emerged.\par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo; Editing by Chris Lewis)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|Z|ABN|D|M|RBN|E|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090523e55k0006r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
