\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  3rd time on Tues to curb HK dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2009\par 08:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details of third \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , May 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a third time on Tuesday, injecting HK$7.13 billion (US$920 million) into the money market in late afternoon to keep an appreciating Hong Kong dollar within its fixed trading band.\par \par \uc2 The move brought the total injections for the day to HK$16.818 billion, including two earlier injections of HK$4.65 billion and HK$5.038 billion as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly hit the top of its trading band at 7.7500 to the U.S. dollar amid strong capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said investors were continuing to pour money into the territory that would eventually head to the Hong Kong and other Asian stock markets.\par \par \uc2 On Monday the HKMA injected HK$10.075 billion to keep the Hong Kong dollar <HKD=> within its band.\par \par \uc2 According to data on Reuters page <HKMAOOC>, the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday will lift the aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- to a record HK$242.207 billion by May 14.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85 to the U.S. dollar. Under the linked exchange rate mechanism, the HKMA is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to keep the trading band intact if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 7.75 or 7.85.\par \par \uc2 By 0912 GMT, it was still quoted at 7.7500. (Reporting by Christina Lo, Editing by Ken Wills and Chris Lewis) ($1=7.75 Hong Kong Dollar)\par \par \uc2 HONGKONG/HKMA (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090512e55c000op\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
