\par\par \b \uc2 DJ HKMA Sells HK$3.875 Bln In NY Session To Defend US Dlr\b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2009\par 18:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold HK$3.875 billion on Tuesday in New York to maintain the USD/HKD trading band under its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, according to data released by the HKMA.\par \par \uc2 This follows an overnight sale before U.S. markets opened of HK$16.818 billion, all to be settled May 14, and extends its recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign.\par \par \uc2 Under \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is pegged at HK$7.80 to the U.S. dollar, but is allowed to trade between HK$7.75 and HK$7.85. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is triggered when the U.S. dollar hits HK$7.7500, the strong side of the Hong Kong dollar's trading band. -By Dan Molinski, Dow Jones Newswires; 201 938-2245; dan.molinski@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Click here to go to Dow Jones NewsPlus, a web front page of today's most important business and market news, analysis and commentary: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnewsplus.com/access/al?rnd=Uf07HjH2E3kguvqrobPF6w%3D%3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.djnewsplus.com/access/al?rnd=Uf07HjH2E3kguvqrobPF6w%3D%3D}}}\uc2 . You can use this link on the day this article is published and the following day.\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2009 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020090512e55c007k9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
