\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar hovers near upper limits, eyes US jobs data\b0\par\par\uc2 628 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2009\par 12:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, May 8 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets in late trade on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Close       Midday      Previous Close\par                        At 0855 GMT At 0454 GMT At 0908 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>       7.7500/01   7.7502/03   7.7503/04\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>   -51/-48     -52/-47     -52/-49\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>     -81/-76     -80/-74     -73/-68\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>     -123/-113   -123/-115   -131/-124\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=> 0.0001/0.0001 0.0001/0.0005 0.0001/0.0001\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>   0.04/0.10   0.04/0.10   0.05/0.14\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=> 0.45/0.60   0.45/0.60   0.50/0.61\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>   0.80/0.90   0.80/0.90   0.80/0.91\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>                1.17/1.27   1.19/1.29\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 * For more live quotes for forwards and interbank rates, click on <FWEN>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar hovered around the top of its trading band against the U.S. dollar on Friday afternoon, buoyed by persistent fund flows into the territory.\par \par \uc2 "Hot money has been flowing in over a week. It looks likely to stay in Hong Kong for investment opportunities," a dealer said.\par \par \uc2 Investors are pouring money into Hong Kong's financial markets on signs China will lead the territory out of the economic downturn, another dealer said.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong's Hang Seng index <.HSI> rose 1 percent to a seven-month high in a seventh session of gains on Friday.\par \par \uc2 * The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) has been actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over the past weeks to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, amid strong capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday and sold HK$4.263 billion ($550 million) for U.S. dollars during New York trading hours. [ID:nHKG346671]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will lift the aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- to a record HK$211.033 billion by next Monday.\par \par \uc2 * HKMA chief Joseph Yam on Friday urged investors to be cautious, saying hefty fund inflows could inflate asset prices in the territory, while local economic conditions remained difficult. [ID:nHKG346756]\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, the HKMA is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar hits 7.75 or 7.75 to keep the band intact.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates softened due to abundant liquidity in the banking system.\par \par \uc2 Three-month Hibor <HIHKD3MD=> was fixed at 0.69321 percent on Friday morning, its lowest level since January 2005.\par \par \uc2 * The discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards narrowed slightly from the previous session, taking their lead from a steady decline in U.S. dollar Libor, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 * Market participants are looking ahead to U.S. non-farm payroll data due at 1230 GMT, for fresh trading clues.\par \par \uc2 Economists polled by Reuters forecast a median 590,000 jobs were lost in April, a mild improvement from a loss of 663,000 jobs in March. But the unemployment rate is seen at 8.9 percent, up from 8.5 percent the previous month. [ECI-US]\par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > IMF says China eeconomic signs encouraging    [ID:nSE0366788]\par  > Q+A-Why is the Hong Kong dollar so strong?    [ID:nHKG275382]\par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|Z|ABN|D|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090511e55800169\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
