\par\par \b \uc2 MONEY MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong \highlight\uc2  interbank rates fall after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 536 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2009\par 08:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * HIBOR edges lower on liquidity injection\par \par \uc2  * U.S. dollar funding costs remain below 1 percent\par \par \uc2  By Umesh Desai\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, May 8 (Reuters) - Hong Kong interbank rates slumped again on Friday as authorities injected liquidity to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its trading band while the cost of borrowing dollars in Asia remained below 1 percent as credit markets heal.\par \par \uc2  Funds are streaming into Hong Kong's financial markets on growing signs China will lead the territory out of the economic downturn and this has pushed the pegged Hong Kong dollar to the top of its trading band.\par \par \uc2  Under Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, which can trade between 7.7500 and 7.8500 to the U.S. dollar, hits the upper or lower limit of its trading band.\par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the HKMA confirmed it injected HK$4.263 billion (US$550 million) into the money market lifting the aggregate balance -- sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- to a record HK$211.033 billion by May 11.\par \par \uc2  The liquidity injection in the local market sent the interbank rates lower.\par \par \uc2  The three-month Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate (HIBOR) was fixed lower at 0.69321 percent from the previous 0.70500 percent.\par \par \uc2  "They are happy with it (the Hong Kong dollar) testing 7.75 and with injecting liquidity especially at a time when there are deflationary forces," said Craig Chan, analyst with Nomura Securities in Singapore.\par \par \uc2  HKMA chief Joseph Yam warned on Thursday hefty fund inflows could inflate asset prices in the territory, while local economic conditions remained difficult. He said the HKMA had issued extra exchange fund bills to absorb some of the funds, otherwise the aggregate balance would have been about HK$300 billion.\par \par \uc2  Asian dollar funding costs remained below 1 percent as dollar London interbank offered rates remained low, indicating banks' increased willingness to lend amid easing credit strains.\par \par \uc2  The 3-month dollar London interbank offered rate (Libor) was fixed at a record low of 0.95625 percent on Thursday.\par \par \uc2  In Asia, three-month dollar funding rates in Singapore fell to 0.95333 percent, down from 0.96857 percent.\par \par \uc2  Australian overnight index swaps showed steady to slightly lower rates for a year ahead, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday slashed its forecasts for economic growth.\par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) sees a sharp contraction this year, but expects record-low interest rates and fiscal stimulus to generate a gradual recovery through 2010.\par \par \uc2  "The RBA sounds like it's comfortably on hold now and perhaps believes it may be done cutting this cycle," said Rob Henderson, head of market economics at National Australia Bank.\par \par \uc2  "But its outlook for inflation also suggests that rates may stay low for longer, with no hike until 2011 even," he added.\par \par \uc2  The RBA skipped a chance to ease at its monthly meeting on Tuesday, after its slashed its cash rate by 425 basis points since September last year to a record low of 3.0 percent.  (Editing by Neil Fullick)    \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-MONEY/ (WRAPUP 1)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090506e556000c9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\