\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar hovers at upper limit, eyes on  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 652 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 2009\par 11:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, April 22 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets in late trade on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Close       Morning     Previous Close\par                        At 0859 GMT At 0317 GMT At 0851 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>       7.7500/01   7.7502/03   7.7502/03\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>   -39/-34     -40/-35     -36/-33\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>     -67/-63     -68/-60     -60/-55\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>     -110/-100   -118/-103   -100/-91\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>   0.01/0.05   0.01/0.05   0.01/0.05\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>   0.18/0.28   0.18/0.28   0.14/0.24\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=> 0.80/0.90   0.75/0.90   0.75/0.88\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>   1.07/1.16   1.07/1.17   1.06/1.16\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>    1.45/1.55   1.45/1.55   1.43/1.53\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 * For more live quotes for forwards and interbank rates, click on <FWEN>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar hovered at the top of its trading band against the U.S. dollar late on Wednesday, which might force the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) to step in again to prevent the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising beyond its fixed range.\par \par \uc2 * The HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and sold a total of HK$2.713 billion ($350 million) for U.S. dollars during the New York trading session on Tuesday as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its upper trading limit at 7.7500. [ID:nHKG124837]\par \par \uc2 * Some dealers said the inflow of funds into the city and strong demand for Hong Kong dollars might be related to an upcoming IPO.\par \par \uc2 China Zhongwang Holdings, Asia's biggest maker of aluminium extrusion products, plans to raise as much as $1.58 billion in a Hong Kong IPO, with a trading debut set for May 8. [ID:nHKG319250]\par \par \uc2 But another dealer at a local bank said aside from recent capital inflows to the equity and property markets, there was also some speculative trading on the yuan <CNY=CFXS>, betting that the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may soon be freely convertible.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is often seen as a proxy for the Chinese yuan.\par \par \uc2 * Although the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit the top of its band at 7.7500 several times on Wednesday afternoon, there was no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the HKMA.\par \par \uc2 * The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, the HKMA is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar hits 7.75 or 7.85, to keep the band intact.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates were mixed.\par \par \uc2 Short-dated interbank rates softened after the HKMA's recent injection.\par \par \uc2 The overnight Hibor <HKDOND=> was fixed at 0.05286 percent, down from 0.06500 percent on Tuesday. The one-week Hibor <HKD1WD=> eased to 0.10357 percent from 0.12071 percent.\par \par \uc2 However, the long-dated interbank rates nudged higher following a rise in interest rate swaps (IRS), one dealer said.\par \par \uc2 The one-year Hibor <HKD1YD=> was fixed at 1.54071 percent, rising from 1.52929 percent on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 * The discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards widened from the previous session, taking cues from softer short-dated interbank rates.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong's Hang Seng index <.HSI> closed 2.67 percent lower on Wednesday as the Shanghai market <.SSEC> pulled back on talk that China's regulators may tighten new lending after a record first quarter for loan growth.\par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo; eding by Chris Lewis)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|Z|ABN|D|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090425e54m00074\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
