\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar hovers near its upper limit, Hibors stable\b0\par\par\uc2 477 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 2009\par 06:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, April 3 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Morning     Previous Close\par                        At 0341 GMT At 0855 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>       7.7503/04   7.7506/07\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>   -46/-41     -45/-41\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>     -82/-72     -78/-72\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>     -140/-130   -137/-127\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>   0.05/0.10   0.03/0.05\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>   0.22/0.32   0.22/0.32\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=> 0.80/0.90   0.80/0.90\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>   1.08/1.18   1.09/1.19\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>    1.41/1.51   1.42/1.52\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 * For more live quotes for forwards and interbank rates, click on <FWEN>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar fell back slightly from the top of its trading band against the U.S. dollar on Friday after the city's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening beyond its fixed range amid capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 * The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> traded between 7.7501 and 7.7504 for much of the session on Friday.\par \par \uc2 * The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during New York trading hours on Thursday and sold HK$3.1 billion ($400 million) for U.S. dollars as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its upper trading limit at 7.7500. [ID:nHKG69906]\par \par \uc2 * Dealers said the USD/HKD spot rate was likely to remain trading in a narrow range, with attention focusing on the stock market's performance.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar gained support recently on equity-related inflow of funds.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, the HKMA is usually obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar hits 7.75 or 7.85, to keep the band intact.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong's Hang Seng index <.HSI> was moving in and out of positive territory on Friday after a sharp 7.4 percent rally the previous session.\par \par \uc2 * Local interbank rates were steady to a touch softer and the discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards widened slightly after the HKMA's latest injection.\par \par \uc2 The three-month Hibor <HKD3MD=> was fixed at 0.90000 percent, compared with 0.90500 percent on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 * Market participants are looking ahead to U.S. non-farm payrolls data due at 1230 GMT, for fresh trading clues.\par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  > Stock market reports and updates:                       [.HK]\par  > Yuan reports and updates:                              [CNY/]\par  > U.S. dollar reports and updates:                [USD/] [FRX/]\par  > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates:           [EMRG/FRX]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christina Lo, Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG/FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|Z|ABN|D|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090406e54300067\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
