\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA sells HK$1.94 bln to curb HK dlr strength\b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Januar 2009\par 03:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Jan 1 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) confirmed on Thursday it had sold HK$1.94 billion ($250 million) for U.S. dollars late on Wednesday in New York trading to curb the strength of the Hong Kong dollar.\par \par \uc2 According to data on Reuters page <HKMAOOC>, the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will lift the aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- to a record HK$175.48 billion by Jan. 5.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been boosted by the liquidation of carry trades, repatriation of capital and inflow of funds into the territory in recent months, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  four times in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday afternoon in Hong Kong trading by selling HK$10.85 billion in total to keep the Hong Kong dollar within its fixed trading band.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar <HKD=> is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85 to the U.S. dollar. Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, the HKMA is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar hits 7.75 or 7.85 to keep the band intact.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 7.7500/01 against the U.S. dollar at 0245 GMT. ($1=HK$7.75) (Reporting by Alison Leung; Editing by Kim Coghill)\par \par \uc2 HONGKONG/HKMA|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090101e5110001m\par }\pag