\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar strong despite c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 679 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2008\par 11:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Dec 12 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Close       Morning     Previous Close\par                        At 0855 GMT At 0325 GMT At 0906 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>       7.7501/02   7.7501/03   7.7502/03\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>   -55/-50     -58/-48     -65/-60\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>     -20/-5      -20/-15     -30/-15\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>       10/30       -5/45      -15/15\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>   0.01/0.15   0.02/0.13   0.05/0.10\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>   0.85/0.95   0.80/0.90   0.90/1.00\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=> 1.55/1.65   1.50/1.60   1.55/1.65\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>   2.05/2.15   2.05/2.15   2.05/2.15\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>    2.20/2.30   2.20/2.30   2.20/2.30\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 * For more live quotes for forwards and interbank rates, click on <FWEN>.\par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar remained at the top of its trading band on Friday, prompting the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) to step in again to stem its appreciation, as investors continued to unwind carry trades.\par \par \uc2 "I think deleveraging is still going on. As the year-end approaches, people want to unwind some positions," said a dealer at a European bank.\par \par \uc2 Another dealer said there was some liquidation of "short Hong Kong dollar, long U.S. dollar" carry trades, probably because some market participants wanted to reduce their portfolio ahead of the year-end.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been repeatedly hitting 7.7500 to the U.S. dollar in the past few days, the upper limit of its pegged trading band, prompting the HKMA to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times. On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold HK$3.1 billion (US$400 million) for U.S. dollars early in the afternoon, bringing its total \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week to HK$10.463 billion.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    As a result, the aggregate balance - sum of balances on\par clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 projected to increase to HK$87.6 billion on Dec. 16 when the transactions are settled.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Local interbank rates extended declines on Friday morning as U.S. dollar Libors fell overnight and after the HKMA's injections into the banking system.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, one- to three-month local interbank rates rebounded slightly in the afternoon amid market jitters on news that U.S. Senate negotiators failed to reach a compromise to bail out ailing U.S. automakers, said a dealer at a local bank.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The one-month Hibor <HKD1MD=> was fixed at 0.89714 percent on Friday morning, compared with 1.04214 percent on Thursday. It rebounded to 0.85/0.95 percent late on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The three-month Hibor <HKD3MD=> rebounded to 1.55/1.65 percent after it was fixed at 1.60286 percent on Friday morning, its lowest level since Feb. 17, 2005.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Hong Kong dollar forwards were bid up due to a narrowing of the HK/US interest rate gap amid expectations that Hong Kong banks might not match an expected U.S. interest rate cut next week, dealers said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. Federal Reserve is widely expected to cut interest rates by at least 50 basis points at its policy meeting on Dec. 15-16.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's curreny peg with the U.S. dollar forces the territory to track U.S. rate moves but local banks have some leeway to lag U.S. rate moves and have ignored most recent cuts in the U.S. federal funds rate.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS >Stock market reports and updates: [.HK] >Yuan reports and updates: [CNY/] >U.S. dollar reports and updates: [USD/] [FRX/] >Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates: [EMRG/FRX] (Reporting by Christina Lo, Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG-FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|Z|ABN|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081215e4cc000rt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
