\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA Yam: Remain Fully Committed To US Dollar Peg\b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2008\par 12:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong monetary chief Joseph Yam reaffirmed his commitment to the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, and said Thursday recent intense \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market should bring down borrowing costs.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  seven times during the Asian trading day Thursday, selling a total of HK$18.21 billion to meet demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has surged to the upper limit of its trading band versus the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Yam said the strong demand was caused by investors deleveraging long U.S. dollar positions and corporations repatriating funds.\par \par \uc2 "We do not notice any market anomalies at the moment," he said.\par \par \uc2 Recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have pushed \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggregate balance to HK$84.27 billion and Yam said there was no upper limit to the balance.\par \par \uc2 He said the large aggregate balance would provide ample liquidity to the banking system and help keep interbank interest rates soft.\par \par \uc2 "This may help translate into lower commercial rates and ease the cost of borrowing," Yam said.\par \par \uc2 In the face of an economic slowdown, the low interest rates are unlikely to fuel excessive credit creation and inflationary concerns, he said.\par \par \uc2 -By Chester Yung, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; chester.yung@dowjones.com [ 20-11-08 1151GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081120e4bk000j1\par }\page