\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar stays strong despite cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2008\par 11:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nov 14 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets late on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Close Mid-day Previous Close\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        At 0915 GMT At 0410 GMT At 0913 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>       7.7502/03   7.7503/05   7.7501/03\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>   -15/-10     -15/-5       -8/2\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>     -20/-10     -20/-10       5/15\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>      -30/20      -25/25       20/40\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>   0.10/0.30   0.10/0.30   0.10/0.30\par  One-month <HKD1MD=>   0.95/1.05   0.95/1.10   0.95/1.15\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=> 2.00/2.15   2.00/2.20   2.00/2.20\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>   2.30/2.50   2.30/2.50   2.30/2.50\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>    2.35/2.55   2.35/2.55   2.35/2.55\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * For more live quotes for forwards and interbank rates, click on <FWEN>.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The Hong Kong dollar remained close to the top of its trading band late on Friday, despite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb its appreciation, as players continued to de-leverage their long U.S. dollar positions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Interbank rates with maturity of less than three months softened slightly and the Hong Kong dollar forwards fell modestly after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's liquidity injection, said a dealer at a local bank.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and injected HK$2.325 billion into the banking system on Friday afternoon as Hong Kong's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit 7.7500 to the U.S. dollar, its upper limit. [ID:nHKU001108]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    As a result, the aggregate balance -- the sum of balances\par on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- was\par projected to increase to HK$51.222 billion on Nov. 18, its\par highest level since mid-May 2004, when the latest transactions\par are settled.\par    The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been boosted in recent weeks by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 unwinding of carry trades amid rising risk aversion. It was trading at 7.7502/03 against the U.S. dollar late on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The one-month interbank rate <HKD1MD=> was quoted at 1.05 percent in late afternoon, below its fixing at 1.10071 percent on Friday morning. The three-month Hibor <HKD3MD=> was quoted at 2.15 percent late on Friday, down from its fixing at 2.19000 percent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, the six-month to one-year interbank rates were barely changed amid thin activity, dealers said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The one-year Hong Kong dollar forwards <HKD1Y=> fell to a discount of 30/10 pips from trading at around par before the HKMA's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the dealer at the local bank said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Some dealers expected the USD/HKD spot rate to stay in a tight range of 7.7500 to 7.7510 next week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * DBS Bank said on Friday it lowered its Hong Kong prime lending rate by 25 basis points to 5.25 percent, effective today following other banks which cut rates on Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The prime rate (or best lending rates) in Hong Kong are currently at 5.00-5.25 percent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * There was little market reaction to third-quarter gross domestic product (GDP) data released late on Friday, which showed Hong Kong slipped into recession. [ID:nHKG81924]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS > Stock market reports and updates: [.HK] > U.S. dollar reports and updates: [USD/] [FRX/] > Yuan reports and updates: [CNY/] > Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates: [EMRG/FRX] (Reporting by Christina Lo, Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG-FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|RBN|Z|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081117e4be000rw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
