\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  three times to curb HK dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2008\par 09:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, background)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nov 11 (Reuters) -TheHong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times in less than an hour on Tuesday afternoon to curb a strong Hong Kong dollar <HKD=>, injecting HK$5.8 billion (US$750 million) to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its pegged trading band.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar, but it can trade between 7.75 and 7.85 and hit its upper limit at 7.7500 repeatedly on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Traders attributed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength to continued unwinding of carry trades, which have become less attractive as interbank rates have been volatile since the global financial crisis deepened two months ago.\par \par \uc2 Previously, investors were selling Hong Kong dollars for U.S. dollars to earn a profit on the interest rate differential between Hong Kong and U.S. dollars. Investors have also been unwinding positions because they need cash after suffering heavy losses in equity and other asset markets, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 "Investment houses and hedge funds are unwinding positions," said Dennis Wong, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Hang Seng Bank.\par \par \uc2 Wong said a narrowing of the spread between short-dated Hong Kong and U.S. interbank rates in the past few days meant there was virtually no demand for U.S. dollars for arbitrage trade.\par \par \uc2 When the Hong Kong dollar hits 7.7500, the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is forced to come in and sell Hong Kong dollars to keep the trading band intact.\par \par \uc2 Over the past few weeks it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit the top of the trading band. In New York trade on Monday, the HKMA injected HK$1.938 billion into the market to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.\par \par \uc2 After the third injection on Tuesday afternoon, the Hong Kong dollar was still at its upper limit, trading at 7.7500/01 at 0954 GMT. (Reporting by Christina Lo and Susan Fenton) (Editing by Anne Marie Roantree)\par \par \uc2 HONGKONG/HKMA (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081111e4bb000ty\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
