\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA Buys HK$3.88 Bln Worth Of USD To Inject Liquidity Wed\b0\par\par\uc2 205 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2008\par 00:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday it bought HK$3.88 billion worth of U.S. dollars during New York trading Wednesday to defend the Hong Kong dollar's peg against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The HKMA's action was triggered by the U.S. dollar hitting HK$7.7500, the lower limit of the trading band under its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, an HKMA spokesman told Dow Jones Newswires. It was the fourth liquidity injection by the HKMA since Friday last week.\par \par \uc2 As a result of the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the aggregate balance in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's banking system will increase to HK$37.82 billion from HK$33.94 billion.\par \par \uc2 At 2350 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at HK$7.7505, slightly down from HK$7.7506 in late Asia trade Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Under Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, the Hong Kong dollar is pegged at HK$7.8000 to the U.S. dollar but is allowed to trade between HK$7.7500 and HK$7.8500.\par \par \uc2 -By Chester Yung, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; chester.yung@dowjones.com [ 05-11-08 2356GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081105e4b5001ah\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
