\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Hong Kong c.bank curbs rise in "safe haven" HK dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Susan Fenton   \par \uc2 806 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2008\par 08:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quote, background)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oct 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday for the first time in nearly a year to stem a rise in the Hong Kong dollar and keep it within official trading limits against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Traders said funds had poured into Hong Kong banks in the past few days as the territory's sound financial system and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to the U.S. dollar were seen as a safe haven, putting upward pressure on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Markets in general are very volatile," said Carlos Cheung, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at \uc2 Bank of East Asia\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Hong Kong is seen as a safe haven as neighbouring countries are quite unstable financially."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA), injected HK$3.877 billion (US$500 million) into the market on Thursday afternoon as the Hong Kong dollar was trading at around 7.7540 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pegged to the U.S. dollar at 7.8, but can trade between 7.85 and 7.75. The HKMA is obliged to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in that range under an arrangement known as the convertibility undertaking.\par \par \uc2 "The Hong Kong dollar exchange rate has strengthened to near the strong side of the convertibility undertaking rate, while short-dated Hong Kong dollar interest rates rose to a premium over U.S. dollar interest rates," an HKMA spokesman told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 "These developments reflect increased demand for Hong Kong dollars. Taking into account market conditions, the HKMA operated within the convertibility zone, purchasing U.S. dollars against Hong Kong dollars," he said.\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL DOWNTURN\par \par \uc2 By late Thursday afternoon, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at around 7.7539 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 "It's still very near the strong side of the convertibility undertaking, so I wouldn't rule out further injections," said Frances Cheung, a strategist at Standard Chartered Bank.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appeal as a safe place to park money was underpinned by the U.S. dollar's rise to a two-year high against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Investors have pulled money out of other Asian markets in the past few days, worried about how the region will be affected by a global economic downturn.\par \par \uc2 Emerging markets generally were perceived as much more risky after it was reported that Pakistan and Hungary sought help from the International Monetary Fund and Argentina nationalized its pension system, seen as an attempt to stave off default.\par \par \uc2 Pakistan said on Thursday it had not formally asked for a loan facility from the IMF.\par \par \uc2 "Even Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with relatively sound fundamentals like the Singapore dollar <SGD=> and Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> have been depreciating this week as fear in emerging markets has increased sharply," said Joe Lo, senior economist at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Hong Kong's financial system is strong and its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg is very stable so it's becoming a safe haven for money in the region."\par \par \uc2 Fitch ratings agency said on Friday that Hong Kong banks are fundamentally sound and should weather challenging economic conditions.\par \par \uc2 Lo said the territory's decision last week to guarantee bank deposits may also be helping boost the Hong Kong dollar, although the impact was limited as only customer deposits are guaranteed not interbank deposits.\par \par \uc2 In offshore trade overnight, the Hong Kong dollar had hit a near one-year high of 7.7516 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 It has stayed on the strong side of its trading band for the past two months as rising risk aversion amid the global credit crisis has discouraged arbitrage trade. Banks' reluctance to lend to each other amid the credit crisis has prompted lenders to sell U.S. dollar positions for Hong Kong dollars to boost liquidity for local \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Arbitrage traders sell Hong Kong dollars for U.S. dollars to make money on the differential between U.S. and Hong Kong dollar interest rates.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the daily one-month Hong Kong interbank offered rate (Hibor) was fixed higher for the first time in a week at 2.92571 percent. Interbank rates had drifted slightly lower this week after action by the HKMA over the past two weeks to ease tight liquidity as banks were cautious about lending amid the global credit crisis.\par \par \uc2 The HKMA said the aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- would increase by HK$3,877 million to HK$17,958 million on Oct. 27 as a result of the fund injection. (Additional reporting by Christina Lo) (Editing by Anne Marie Roantree and Jacqueline Wong)\par \par \uc2 HONGKONG/HKMA (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081023e4an000js\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
