\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA:Public Concerns About Bank Of East Asia "Largely Subsided"\b0\par\par\uc2 210 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2008\par 12:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday that public worries about \uc2 Bank of East Asia Ltd\uc2 . (0023.HK) had "largely subsided" and added its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market hadn't targeted any specific institution.\par \par \uc2 The HMKA said \uc2 Bank of East Asia\uc2  remained in good financial health and had been able to handle a run on the bank that began Wednesday as hundreds of depositors lined up to get their money.\par \par \uc2 "The bank has been able to handle the unusual situation," the HKMA, Hong Kong's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said in a statement. The run on the bank was caused by text message rumors about its stability that were rejected by the bank, the HKMA and \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial secretary.\par \par \uc2 The HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market early Thursday, buying HK$3.883 billion in U.S. dollars, and its statement said the move had been made to ease interbank liquidity.\par \par \uc2 The HKMA will continue to monitor the situation closely, and will deploy further measures to inject liquidity into the market if needed, the statement said.\par \par \uc2 -By Jackie Cheung, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; jackie.cheung@dowjones.com [ 25-09-08 1037GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080925e49p000jv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
