\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE HKMA Investment Returns Hit 9 Year-high Of 11.8%   \b0\par\par\uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2008\par 13:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from HKMA chief executive, exchange fund's total asset value.)   \par \par \uc2 By Chester Yung   \par \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Monday its investment portfolio posted a nine-year high return of 11.8%, but added that such a performance could be hard to repeat this year.   \par \par \uc2 "Concerns about widening credit spreads, the profitability of financial institutions and the risks to U.S. economic growth will continue to affect sentiment," HKMA Chief Executive Joseph Yam told a news conference.   \par \par \uc2 Yam also said "unpredictable administrative measures" in mainland China can affect the investment environment.   \par \par \uc2 Yam didn't elaborate, but Hong Kong's market got a big lift in August when China said it would allow individuals in the mainland to purchase shares directly in Hong Kong, a deal that has become known as the "through train."   \par \par \uc2 Since then, there has been no word on when the program could start, stirring up much speculation about delays.   \par \par \uc2 The HKMA said Monday the Exchange Fund posted unaudited investment income of HK$142.2 billion (US$18.2 billion) last year, up from HK$103.8 billion in 2006. Net investment income in 2007 jumped to HK$132.2 billion from the previous year's HK$93.5 billion.   \par \par \uc2 The overall rate of return was 11.8%, the highest since the fund made 12.1% in 1998. The latest return was based largely on gains in local equities and bonds and compared with a return of 9.5% in 2006.   \par \par \uc2 Yam said market volatility is likely to remain high, given developments in international financial markets and the likely continued macroeconomic tightening in China. The Exchange Fund is used to manage Hong Kong's exchange rate and maintain financial stability. Its total assets stood at HK$1.42 trillion by the end of December, up from HK$1.18 trillion a year earlier.   \par \par \uc2 The fund made HK$55.8 billion, or about 40% of last year's gains, in the local stock market. It gained HK$61 billion from bonds and other investments. It generated a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  gain of HK$18.7 billion in 2007 from its holdings in different \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , mainly as a result of the appreciation of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar. Hong Kong pegs its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong government's share of the Exchange Fund's gains amounted to HK$27.6 billion, higher than the government's February 2007 estimate of HK$26 billion.   \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong places money from fiscal surpluses into the fund.   \par \par \uc2 Facing questions from reporters, Yam said there is no sign of massive capital outflow from Hong Kong despite a recent slide in the territory's stock market. Hong Kong blue chips added to their recent losses by plunging 5.5% Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Yam said the Hong Kong dollar has "remained stable" against the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The HKMA is committed to keeping the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading within a band of 7.75 to 7.85 to the U.S. dollar. It had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  five times in October when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar tested the upper limit of the band.   \par \par \uc2 -By Chester Yung, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; chester.yung@dowjones.com [ 21-01-08 1206GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080121e41l000qk\par }\page {