\par\par \b \uc2 IMF urges HK to fix anomalies to guard dollar peg   \b0\par\par\uc2 446 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2007\par 08:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Nov 20 (Reuters) - The International Monetary Fund has urged Hong Kong to look at ways to reduce anomalies between its money and exchange rate markets to prevent speculative pressure on the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg.   \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong interbank rates, which typically trade below U.S. dollar rates, recently shot up partly because of fund inflows for big initial public offerings by mainland Chinese firms.   \par \par \uc2 The high interest rates, and rapid fund flows into local equities, pushed the Hong Kong dollar <HKD=> to the top of its trading band for the first time last month, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the peg.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar but since 2005 has been allowed to trade between 7.75 and 7.85   \par \par \uc2 "The authorities could consider reinforcing the link between changes in the aggregate balance and Hong Kong dollar interest rates, as well as look to improve the management of liquidity within the financial system," the IMF said in a report on Hong Kong circulated on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 "Doing so could help to avoid further episodic anomalies between the Hong Kong dollar exchange rate and interest rate movements, which is a potential source of market speculation about the longevity of the linked exchange rate system."   \par \par \uc2 Joseph Yam, chief executive of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told legislators this month that there was room to enhance the peg -- known as the linked exchange rate system -- without fundamentally changing it, but did not say how.   \par \par \uc2 Investment bank  \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  said his remarks suggested the HKMA would look at ways to improve efficiency of the money market.   \par \par \uc2 Interbank rates were pushed up to their highest levels in six years last month as strong demand for Hong Kong dollars for IPOs tightened liquidity and as banks were cautious about lending in the wake of a global credit squeeze.   \par \par \uc2 A strong stock market pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to test its limit at 7.75 and some speculators emerged, betting the territory could abandon its link with the U.S. dollar or widen the trading band.   \par \par \uc2 Yam said the government had no intention of changing the peg or widening the band and the IMF in its report supported Hong Kong's commitment to the linked exchange rate system.   \par \par \uc2 Rates have now dropped below U.S. dollar rates and the Hong Kong dollar is back within its trading band. It was quoted at 7.7812/13 on Tuesday afternoon. (Reporting by Susan Fenton, editing by Dominic Whiting)   \par \par \uc2 HONGKONG/IMF|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071120e3bk000jx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
