\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar hits 1-month low, interbank rates fall   \b0\par\par\uc2 814 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2007\par 10:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Nov 2 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets in late trade on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       Close        Morning      Previous Close\par                       At 0853 GMT  At 0323 GMT  At 0912 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>      7.7620/21    7.7615/16    7.7557/60\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>  -178/-173   -168/-161   -121/-111\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>    -285/-275   -263/-247   -220/-212\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>     -470/-455   -450/-430   -430/-415\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>   1.80/2.00   2.25/2.50   2.50/2.75\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=> 3.95/4.00   3.98/4.03   4.18/4.23\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>   4.01/4.06   4.01/4.06   4.18/4.23\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>    3.97/4.02   4.01/4.06   4.07/4.12\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 * For more live quotes for both forwards and interbank rates, click on <FWEN>.   \par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar <HKD=> is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar but since May 2005 has been allowed to trade between 7.75 and 7.85.   \par \par \uc2 * The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell for a second day on Friday, kept at bay by arbitrage trade, which was boosted by a further drop in interbank rates. The overnight interbank rate hit a two-year low after liquidity in the banking system increased.   \par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar fell to a one-month low of 7.7632 against the U.S. dollar before rebounding to 7.7620/21 at 0853 GMT, but was still weaker than 7.7557/60 in late Thursday trade in Asia.   \par \par \uc2 * One trader at a European bank said sell orders for U.S. dollars diminished after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (HKMA) aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past two weeks and as speculation against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg retreated following the Hong Kong government's reaffirmation of its commitment to the linked exchange rate system.   \par \par \uc2 The trader said the Hong Kong dollar was likely to head towards 7.7650 to the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 * Dealers said arbitrage trade had become attractive again as local interbank rates had fallen below U.S. dollar interbank rates by at least 1 percentage point.   \par \par \uc2 Arbitrage traders can make a profit from an interest rate spread by selling Hong Kong dollars for the greenback.   \par \par \uc2 Interbank rates have fallen as the aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- increased to HK$10.619 billion on Friday from the previous day's close at HK$2.792 billion, after settlement on Friday of the HKMA's injection of funds on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 * The overnight interbank rate fell to 1.80/2.00 percent, its lowest level since November 2005, according to Reuters data.   \par \par \uc2 The one-week rate slipped to 2.95/3.00 percent from 3.75/3.80 percent. The one-month rate decreased further to 3.50/3.55 percent in late afternoon trade, versus 3.53/3.58 percent late in the morning and down from Thursday's close at 3.93/4.00 percent.   \par \par \uc2 The three-month rate has fallen to 3.95/4.00 percent from a peak of 5.45 percent on Oct. 17.   \par \par \uc2 As a result, the discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards widened. The one-week forwards <HKDSW=> were trading at a discount of 25/20 pips, compared with Thursday's close of 15/10 pips. The discount on one-year forwards <HKD1Y=> widened to 470/455 pips from 430/415 pips.   \par \par \uc2 * A correction in the stock market had little effect on the Hong Kong dollar, some traders said.   \par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS   \par \par \uc2 * HONG KONG - Hong Kong stocks dropped more than 3 percent on Friday as a slide in global equities prompted investors to pocket recent gains, with shares in the city's property developers hit especially hard following a record-breaking rally.   \par \par \uc2 Stock market reports and updates: [.HK]   \par \par \uc2 - - - -   \par \par \uc2 * LONDON - The dollar edged down towards record lows against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday as investors looked to a key U.S. jobs report for clues on whether growth is soft enough to warrant another rate cut next month.   \par \par \uc2 U.S. dollar reports and updates: [USD/] [FRX/]   \par \par \uc2 - - - -   \par \par \uc2 * SHANGHAI - China's yuan weakened slightly against the dollar on Friday as the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used its mid-point to curb the yuan's gains, after allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strike a series of post-revaluation highs this week.   \par \par \uc2 Yuan reports and updates: [CNY/]   \par \par \uc2 - - - -   \par \par \uc2 * SINGAPORE - Sliding stocks gave investors an excuse to book profits from recent rallies in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, while investors turned to U.S. jobs data later in the day for fresh clues on the Federal Reserve's monetary policy.   \par \par \uc2 Emerging Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reports and updates: [EMRG/FRX]   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG-FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071105e3b2000tm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
