\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar falls further after Yam comments   \b0\par\par\uc2 943 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2007\par 11:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Nov 1 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets in late trade on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Close Morning Previous Close   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       At 0912 GMT  At 0422 GMT  At 0930 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>      7.7557/60    7.7532/35    7.7500/01\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=> -121/-111    -124/-117    -100/-90\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>   -220/-212    -235/-225    -200/-190\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>    -430/-415    -465/-435    -430/-410\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>   2.50/2.75   3.40/3.50   3.50/4.00\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=> 4.18/4.23   4.23/4.28   4.35/4.40\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>   4.18/4.23   4.19/4.24   4.30/4.32\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>    4.07/4.12   4.09/4.14   4.10/4.15\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * For more live quotes for both forwards and interbank rates, click on <FWEN>.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The Hong Kong dollar <HKD=> is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar but since May 2005 has been allowed to trade between 7.75 and 7.85.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell against the U.S. dollar on Thursday after the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively injected liquidity on Wednesday to defend the peg.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It extended losses in late trade after Joseph Yam, the head of the HKMA, said the government had no plans to re-peg the Hong Kong dollar at a different level or widen its trading band. For further details, double click [nHKG269070].   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was trading at 7.7557/60 against the U.S. dollar at 0912 GMT, its lowest level since Oct. 17, down from 7.7500/01 in late Wednesday trade in Asia.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Dealers also attributed the fall in the Hong Kong dollar to the re-emergence of some arbitrage trades as local interbank rates fell below U.S. dollar interbank rates.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "After hefty injections by the HKMA, short-dated forwards are returning to a discount from a premium, implying the cost of carry is favourable to buy back the U.S. dollar," said a dealer at a European bank.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The one-week Hong Kong dollar forwards <HKDSW=> were trading at a discount of 15/10 pips on Thursday, compared with a premium of 5/10 pips before the HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on Wednesday afternoon.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  five times on Wednesday, selling a total of HK$7.828 billion (US$1 billion) to stem the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar's strength.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Wednesday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will lift the aggregate balance\par -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks\par with the HKMA -- to HK$10.619 billion after settlement on Nov.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2, from HK$2.792 billion on Thursday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The HKMA dismissed a report by U.S.-based research house Medley Global Advisors, circulating on Wednesday, that Hong Kong officials had lobbied Beijing to allow changes to the Hong Kong dollar peg. The report said they had advocated either widening the trading band or pegging it with a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but Beijing had refused to consider any changes.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * However, Eric Wong, an executive director at  \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  Investment Research, told a news conference on Thursday that Hong Kong should consider depegging its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , or at least setting up an advisory board to discuss the issue, because a weakening U.S. dollar would increase inflation in Hong Kong and asset prices would rise further.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Falling interbank rates prompted local banks to cut their best lending rates on Thursday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (For a full story, double click on [nHKG261283].)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The one-month rate was quoted at 3.93/4.00 percent in late afternoon trade, a level not seen since February. It had fallen by 70 basis points before the HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The three-month rate fell to 4.18/4.23 percent, its lowest since May, down from Wednesday's close at 4.35/4.40 percent.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong tends to follow U.S. rates because its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is pegged to the U.S. dollar, but banks also base their rate movements on market liquidity conditions.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Hong Kong dollar forwards moved in tandem with interbank rates.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The discount on one-month forwards <HKD1Y=> widened to 46/41 pips from Wednesday's close at 30/25 pips. The discount on one-year forwards <HKD1Y=> was trading at 430/415 pips late in the afternoon, versus 480/460 pips in early morning trade and little changed from Wednesday's close at 430/410 pips.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * HONG KONG - Hong Kong-listed China plays ended up 0.4 percent on Thursday, having touched a new high during the day, as oil-related shares rallied on record crude prices and a decision by China to lift domestic fuel prices.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock market reports and updates: [.HK]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * LONDON - The dollar recovered from a record low against the euro on Thursday after the Federal Reserve cut rates as expected the previous day but dampened expectations of further monetary policy easing this year.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. dollar reports and updates: [USD/] [FRX/]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * SHANGHAI - China's yuan hit a fresh post-revaluation high against the dollar on Thursday for the fourth straight day, after the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again set a higher reference rate for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yuan reports and updates: [CNY/]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * SINGAPORE - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose on Thursday after the Federal Reserve's expected rate cut further eroded the dollar's yield appeal, while investors awaited new data on the U.S. economy and further policy easing.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates: [EMRG/FRX]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG-FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071104e3b100079\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
