\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar hits 2-week low, interbank rates fall   \b0\par\par\uc2 940 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2007\par 05:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Nov 1 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets as of late Thursday morning.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       Morning      Previous Close\par                       At 0422 GMT  At 0930 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>      7.7532/35    7.7500/01\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=> -124/-117    -100/-90\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>   -235/-225    -200/-190\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>    -465/-435    -430/-410\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>   3.40/3.50   3.50/4.00\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=> 4.23/4.28   4.35/4.40\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>   4.19/4.24   4.30/4.32\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>    4.09/4.14   4.10/4.15\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 * For more live quotes for both forwards and interbank rates, click on <FWEN>.   \par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar <HKD=> is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar but since May 2005 has been allowed to trade between 7.75 and 7.85.   \par \par \uc2 * The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a two-week low against the U.S. dollar on Thursday after the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) aggressively injected liquidity on Wednesday to defend the peg, pushing interbank rates down to their lowest levels in months.   \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar fell as low as 7.7547 before rebounding to 7.7532/35 at 0422 GMT, but was still down from 7.7500/01 in late Asia trade on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 * One dealer at a European bank attributed the fall to a softening in interbank rates, prompting some players to re-enter carry trade.   \par \par \uc2 "After hefty injections by the HKMA, short-dated forwards are returning to a discount from a premium, implying the cost of carry is favourable to buy back the U.S. dollar," the dealer said.   \par \par \uc2 The one-week Hong Kong dollar forwards <HKDSW=> was quoted at a discount of 7 pips versus Wednesday's morning at a premium of 8 pips, the dealer added.   \par \par \uc2 * The HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  five times on Wednesday, selling a total of HK$7.828 billion (US$1 billion) to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's strength.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Wednesday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will lift the aggregate balance\par -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks\par with the HKMA -- to HK$10.619 billion after settlement on Nov. 2,\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from HK$2.792 billion on Thursday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The Hong Kong dollar suffered upward pressure on Wednesday amid speculative trades on the peg regime, while the HKMA reaffirmed it is committed to the linked exchange rate system.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some speculative pressure had added to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength on Wednesday after hedge fund Medley Global Advisors published a report saying Hong Kong officials had lobbied Beijing to allow changes to the Hong Kong dollar peg.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The report said they had advocated either by widening the trading band or moving to peg it with a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but Beijing had refused to consider any changes.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The HKMA said, however, the report was unfounded and HKMA Chief Executive Joseph Yam repeated on Thursday that the Hong Kong government was committed to the peg, and rumours that officials were lobbying Beijing had no foundation.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Some dealers expect the Hong Kong dollar will remain strong in the near term, partly due to a steady inflow of foreign investment funds into the city amid a buoyant equity market and frenzied IPO activity.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Interbank rates declined further on Thursday after HKMA Wednesday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The one-week rate slipped to 3.85/3.90 percent from 4.35/4.30 percent late on Wednesday. The one-month rate fell to 4.03/4.08 percent, its lowest level since late March, from Wednesday's close at 4.35/4.40 percent. The three-month rate eased to 4.23/4.28 percent, a level not seen since early May, down from 4.35/4.40 percent late on Wednesday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Hong Kong dollar forwards moved in tandem with interbank rates. The discount on one-year forwards <HKD1Y=> widened to 480/460 pips before settling at 465/435 pips on profit taking, compared with Wednesday's close at 430/410 pips.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * A fall in interbank rates has led a local bank to cut its best lending rate.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings Plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Thursday it would lower its best lending rate in Hong Kong by 25 basis points to 7.27 percent, effective Friday. [ID:nHKU000898].   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers expect other banks will follow the rate cut.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The U.S. Federal Reserve cut interest rates by 25 basis points on Wednesday, as expected.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong tends to follow the U.S. rates move because its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is pegged to the U.S. dollar.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The HKMA early on Thursday matched the Fed's move by cutting the base rate at its discount window from which banks may borrow overnight liquidity to 6.00 percent from 6.25 percent.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * HONG KONG - Hong Kong stocks rose on Thursday after the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut interest rates, with oil issues leading the way after crude prices hit new highs.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock market reports and updates: [.HK]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * TOKYO - The dollar crawled up against the euro on Thursday after hitting a record low the previous day as the Federal Reserve's expected interest rate cut further eroded the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's appeal to foreign investors.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. dollar reports and updates: [USD/] [FRX/]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yuan reports and updates: [CNY/]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * SINGAPORE - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose versus a broadly weaker dollar on Thursday after a Federal Reserve rate cut made their yields more attractive.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports and updates: [EMRG/FRX]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG-FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071104e3b100027\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
