\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA Yam:US Dlr Peg Working Well For Exchange Rate Stability   \b0\par\par\uc2 238 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2007\par 09:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chief Executive Joseph Yam said in his weekly Internet column Thursday that the Hong Kong government has no plans to re-peg the local dollar at a different level against the U.S. dollar or widen the current trading band.   \par \par \uc2 "The linked exchange rate system has been functioning well to deliver exchange-rate stability," Yam said in his column, which was published on the HKMA's Web site.   \par \par \uc2 Under Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, the Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar, but is allowed to trade between 7.75 and 7.85. When the Hong Kong dollar reaches the limits of its trading band, the HKMA can be expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar had hovered near the top end of its trading band to the U.S. dollar Wednesday, prompting the HKMA to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market five times to curb the appreciating local dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Yam said the HKMA will buy more U.S. dollars by injecting more Hong Kong dollar liquidity if the strong side of the trading band is further "triggered."   \par \par \uc2 But he added the interest rate discount that has emerged "may be enough to generate the counterbalancing outflow."   \par \par \uc2 -By Jeffrey Ng, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; jeffrey.ng@dowjones.com [ 01-11-07 0827GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020071101e3b1000lu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
