\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ UPDATE: HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  Twice; Traders Expect More Action   \b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2007\par 10:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2007, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds second \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analyst comments.) By Jackie Cheung Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday, buying HK$3.875 billion worth of U.S. dollars to halt the Hong Kong dollar's rise and keep it within its allowable trading band to the U.S. unit.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said they expect further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the city's de-facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term amid expectations the U.S. Federal Reserve will cut its key interest rates later Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 'I expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will typically come in a wave, rather than being one-off,' said  \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  analyst Claudio Piron. 'We'll likely continue to see more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  going forward.'   \par \par \uc2 Under \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, the Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but is allowed to trade between 7.75 and 7.85. When the Hong Kong dollar reaches the limits of its trading band, the HKMA can be expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The HKMA declined to provide the level at which it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday, but traders said they believed it was 7.75.   \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar had hovered near the top end of its trading band to the U.S. dollar all morning Wednesday, before the HKMA stepped in first with a HK$3.1 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Less than half an hour later, it made a HK$775 million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Wednesday's moves follow two \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the HKMA last week, which were its first such actions in more than two years.   \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar has been rising against the U.S. dollar as investors pour money into the red hot Hong Kong stock market, and the U.S. dollar falls against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The market widely expects the Federal Open Market Committee to cut U.S. interest rates by a quarter point or even a half point later Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 At 0800 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at HK$7.7501, down from HK$7.7507 late Tuesday and near the lower limit of its trading band with the Hong Kong unit. -By Jackie Cheung, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; jackie.cheung@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -0-    \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020071031e3av005bp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
