\par\par \b \uc2 HK interbank rates fall after c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 831 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2007\par 11:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oct 31 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets in late trade on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Close Morning Previous Close   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       At 0930 GMT  At 0307 GMT  At 0855 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>      7.7500/01    7.7502/03    7.7502/03\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>  -100/-90     -35/-28     -54/-49\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>    -200/-190   -110/-100   -127/-117\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>     -430/-410   -280/-260   -300/-280\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>   3.50/4.00   4.80/4.95   3.55/3.75\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=> 4.35/4.40   4.63/4.68   4.60/4.65\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>   4.30/4.32   4.47/4.52   4.44/4.49\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>    4.10/4.15   4.22/4.27   4.21/4.26\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * For more live quotes for both forwards and interbank rates, click on <FWEN>.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The Hong Kong dollar <HKD=> is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar but since May 2005 has been allowed to trade between 7.75 and 7.85.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Interbank rates fell sharply on Wednesday afternoon after the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) aggressively injected liquidity to keep the peg intact and to ease demand for funds.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The one-week interbank rate was quoted at 4.35/4.40 percent, slipping from 4.95/5.00 percent in the late morning. The one-month rate declined to 4.35/4.40 percent, down 28 basis points from late morning. The three-month rate fell to 4.35/4.40 percent in late afternoon from Tuesday's close at 4.60/4.65 percent.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The HKMA sold a total of HK$6.2 billion worth of the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for U.S. dollar on Wednesday to stem the Hong Kong dollar's strength. The aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- was projected to increase to HK$8.992 billion after settlement on Nov. 2, from HK$2.792 billion on Wednesday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers said the strong demand for Hong Kong dollars on Wednesday was partly due to the settlement of China e-commerce firm  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alibaba.com\f28 \uc2 \f2 's IPO subscription as well as capital inflows for a spate of IPOs in November.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (For a related story on the Hong Kong dollar, double click on [ID:nHKG269940].)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The Hong Kong dollar was trading at 7.7500/01 against the U.S. dollar at 0850 GMT.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers expect the HKMA to step into the market again as the Hong Kong dollar remains near its upper trading limit to the U.S. dollar.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Under the exchange rate mechanism, the HKMA is committed to buy U.S. dollars from licenced banks in exchange for Hong Kong dollars if the spot rate hits 7.75.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Hong Kong dollar forwards moved in tandem with interbank rates. The discount on one-year forwards <HKD1Y=> widened to 430/410 pips late on Wednesday, versus 280/260 pips in late morning and Tuesday's close of 300/280 pips.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Market participants were awaiting the outcome of the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) meeting later in the day. The Fed is widely expected to cut interest rates by 25 basis points when it concludes a two-day policy meeting on Wednesday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong tends to track U.S. interest rate moves because its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is pegged to the U.S. dollar, but banks have some leeway in setting rates depending on liquidity.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Fed's decision is due at 1815 GMT (2:15 a.m. Hong Kong time on Thursday).   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Dealers said there was a higher chance for banks here to follow an expected rate cut in the United States after the HKMA injections.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * HONG KONG - Hong Kong blue chips fell 0.9 percent on Wednesday as caution over a U.S. interest rate decision pushed down property shares, which had surged on expectations of a rate cut.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock market reports and updates: [.HK]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * LONDON - The dollar hit a record low versus a basket of major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the fourth trading day in a row on Wednesday, with investors poised for a U.S. rate cut later in the session and possible hints of more cuts to come.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. dollar reports and updates: [USD/] [FRX/]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * SHANGHAI - China's yuan <CNY=CFXS> hit a fresh post-revaluation high against the dollar on Wednesday after the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  indicated it was willing to permit more appreciation in the short term by setting a higher mid-point.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yuan reports and updates: [CNY/]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - - - -   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * SINGAPORE - The South Korean won jumped to a new 10-year high on Wednesday despite jitters about official \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , leading Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher versus a beleaguered dollar ahead of an expected Federal Reserve rate cut.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 