\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-HK spends $1 bln easing HKD, waves off de-pegging talk   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Christina Lo   \par \uc2 764 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2007\par 08:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Add details, latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market comments)   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oct 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the equivalent of around US$1 billion in Hong Kong dollars on Wednesday as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bumped up repeatedly against the ceiling of its trading band with the weakening U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  five times in three hours, selling HK$7.828 billion as it stepped up efforts to temper the strength of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar has clung stubbornly to its two-year-old ceiling of 7.75 against the U.S. dollar, which hit a record low against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the fourth trading day in a row on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Funds flowing into Hong Kong, plus rising import costs from the Chinese mainland, are stirring talk that the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to drop a two-decade-old peg against the U.S. dollar, or at least widen the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's wafer-thin trading band.   \par \par \uc2 Fuelling upward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was demand to buy shares in the initial public offering of China e-commerce firm  \uc2 Alibaba.com.\par \par \uc2 The US$1.49 billion offer has attracted about US$100 billion in orders from institutions alone, sustaining inflows from outside Hong Kong into Asia's second-largest stock market.   \par \par \uc2 Traders and analysts saw little pure speculative buying. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reaffirmed its commitment to the peg, adding it had no intention of lobbying Beijing at present for permission to drop the link despite talk to the contrary.   \par \par \uc2 "If there's any speculative buying, it wasn't big. The Alibaba subscriptions need Hong Kong dollars. Local interest rates are high now, but will come down after the Alibaba settlement," said Andrew Fung, head of investment and insurance at Hang Seng Bank.   \par \par \uc2 "The stock market is so hot these days."   \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pegged at 7.8 per U.S. dollar but since May 2005 has been allowed to trade between 7.75 and 7.85. Under the exchange rate mechanism, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is committed to buying U.S. dollars from licensed banks in exchange for Hong Kong dollars if the spot rate hits 7.75.   \par \par \uc2 Indded, the HKMA had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice last week, selling a total of HK$1.55 billion for U.S. dollars.   \par \par \uc2 By 0938 GMT, the Hong Kong dollar was trading at 7.7500/01 against the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 RUMOURS FLY   \par \par \uc2 ING expects Hong Kong to prise the trading range wider in time, possibly at the upper limit. But economists said abandoning the peg, which stood firm through the Asian financial crisis of 1997/98 and the SARS epidemic of 2003/04, was unlikely.   \par \par \uc2 Talk of an imminent adjustment -- which includes speculation of an adjustment of the exchange rate, or a link to the Chinese yuan -- picked up in volume after government sources said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Joseph Yam would step down in 2009.   \par \par \uc2 "The government is fully committed to the maintenance of the linked exchange rate system," a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman said, repeating comments on the peg over the past week. "We have no intention to introduce any changes to the system."   \par \par \uc2 Reuters data showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday for the first time shortly after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its ceiling at 0705 GMT, selling HK$3.1 billion worth of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It followed with four other actions over the next few hours.   \par \par \uc2 Before the peg speculation re-emerged in past months, a buoyant stock market, frenzied IPO activity and a weakening U.S. dollar had already attracted funds into the city.   \par \par \uc2 "A strengthening yuan, appreciation of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the greenback, plus talk of Yam's departure, are all triggering talk of a change in the peg," a trader with a foreign bank said. "As the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds firm, that's attracting an inflow of capital."   \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's blue-chip Hang Seng Index has risen about 50 percent in the past two months, after China said it would let mainland individuals buy into Hong Kong stocks. Now, mounting inflation is lending weight to arguments for a peg abolition.   \par \par \uc2 Others argue that inflation has quickened this year, partly because of the rising cost of Chinese imports as the yuan climbs in value, but remains relatively moderate at below 3 percent. ($1=HK$7.750) (Additional reporting by Alison Leung)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HKMA/ (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071031e3av000tq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
