\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar retreats slightly after HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 737 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2007\par 12:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oct 26 (Reuters) - The following is a snapshot of Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets in late trade on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       Close        Morning      Previous Close\par                       At 0856 GMT  At 0316 GMT  At 0923 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>      7.7507/08    7.7501/02    7.7509/10\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month <HKD3M=>  -60/-55      -54/-49     -33/-25\par  Six-month <HKD6M=>   -127/-121    -124/-114    -85/-75\par  One-year <HKD1Y=>    -285/-270    -278/-248   -220/-200\par  INTERBANK RATES (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight <HKDOND=>   4.60/4.80   4.75/4.95   3.50/3.75\par  Three-month <HKD3MD=> 4.63/4.68   4.73/4.78   4.78/4.83\par  Six-month <HKD6MD=>   4.43/4.48   4.50/4.55   4.60/4.65\par  One-year <HKD1YD=>    4.28/4.33   4.32/4.37   4.38/4.43\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 * For more live quotes for both forwards and interbank rates, click on <FWEN>.   \par \par \uc2 * The Hong Kong dollar <HKD=> is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85.   \par \par \uc2 * Strong demand for funds from investors to buy stocks pushed the Hong Kong dollar to 7.75, its upper limit against the U.S. dollar, late on Friday morning and prompted the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) to inject liquidity to keep the peg intact.   \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar then retreated slightly but some dealers said sentiment in the stock market remains robust and expected the HKMA could come into the market again to ease demand for funds.   \par \par \uc2 (For a related story on the Hong Kong dollar, double click on [ID:nHKG171802].)   \par \par \uc2 * The HKMA, the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sold HK$775 million worth of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for U.S. dollars on Friday, injecting funds for the second time this week.   \par \par \uc2 Friday's injection will lift the aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- to HK$2.852 billion after settlement on Oct. 30, from HK$2.032 billion on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 * The injection by the HKMA helped to push down local interbank rates and triggered a sell-off in Hong Kong dollar forwards, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 The one-week interbank rate eased to 4.85/4.90 percent late on Friday from 4.95/5.00 percent in late morning. The one-month rate slipped to 4.58/4.63 percent from 4.68/4.73 percent in late morning and down from Thursday's close at 4.80/4.85 percent. The three-month rate eased to 4.63/4.68 percent from 4.78/4.83 percent late on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the discount on one-year forwards <HKD1Y=> widened to 300 pips before settling at 290/270 pips in late afternoon, compared with 220/200 pips late on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 *  \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  said in a research note that the increase in interbank liquidity would push interbank rates lower and reduce banks' funding costs.   \par \par \uc2 The investment bank said banks were therefore now more likely to follow a widely expected quarter point cut in U.S. interest rates when the Federal Reserve meets next Tuesday-Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong tends to track U.S. interest rate moves because its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pegged to the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 MARKET/ECONOMIC NEWS   \par \par \uc2 * HONG KONG - Hong Kong blue chips jumped 1.8 percent on Friday, staying firmly above the key 30,000 level for the first time, with property stocks hitting records, stoked by a weak U.S. dollar and speculation of a rate cut by the Federal Reserve, which meets next week.   \par \par \uc2 Stock market reports and updates: [.HK]   \par \par \uc2 - - - -   \par \par \uc2 * LONDON - The dollar fell to fresh record lows against the euro and a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday as investors, faced with a run of weak U.S. economic data, braced for a Federal Reserve interest rate cut next week.   \par \par \uc2 U.S. dollar reports and updates: [USD/] [FRX/]   \par \par \uc2 - - - -   \par \par \uc2 * SHANGHAI - China's yuan <CNY=CFXS> fell against the dollar on Friday, pushed down by outflows of funds despite a higher yuan mid-point set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Yuan reports and updates: [CNY/]   \par \par \uc2 - - - -   \par \par \uc2 * SINGAPORE - The Singapore dollar, Korean won and Malaysian ringgit hit fresh 10-year highs on Friday after some Asian central banks to step into the market.   \par \par \uc2 Emerging Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reports and updates: [EMRG/FRX]   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG-FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071029e3aq00250\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
