\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-HK dollar hits lowest level in more than two decades   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Susan Fenton   \par \uc2 572 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 2007\par 09:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quote, details)   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Aug 1 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar <HKD=> on Wednesday hit its lowest level since it was pegged to the U.S. dollar more than two decades ago as investors fled the local stock market and reduced their exposure to Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid to 7.83 to the U.S. dollarin afternoon trade after the stock market's benchmark Hang Seng Index <.HSI> plunged 3.2 percent on the day, on record turnover, as concerns grew that woes in the U.S. subprime mortgage sector were having an impact overseas. For details, click on [.HK]   \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar has been linked to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1983. It is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85.   \par \par \uc2 "Funds are flowing out of Asia, including Hong Kong and that is being reflected in the Hong Kong dollar as well," said Nizam Idris, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 UBS\uc2  in Singapore.   \par \par \uc2 "We're seeing a general re-rating of risk and Asian markets that have seen significant inflows are seeing a reversal of that. But Asian fundamentals are strong and once the market gets a lot more balanced fundamentals will be of some support in Asia, Hong Kong included."   \par \par \uc2 Support for the Hong Kong dollar at 7.83 appeared to be firm. However, analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could break that level in coming weeks amid continued re-rating of investor risk appetite across Asia. They said it was unlikely to fall as low as 7.85. If it does hit that level the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band.   \par \par \uc2 Funds have flooded into \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  stocks this year, pushing the market to all-time highs, amid keen investor interest in Chinese companies and a robust Hong Kong economy, which is forecast to grow 5.5 percent this year, according to a Reuters poll.   \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's China enterprises index <.HSCE> of Chinese companies listed on the Hong Kong exchange slid 3.9 percent on Wednesday, after plunging more than 5 percent in early afternoon trade.   \par \par \uc2 While demand for Hong Kong dollars for stock purchases has been strong this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weakened as speculative fund flows anticipating Hong Kong would adjust its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to trade more in line with China's appreciating yuan have disappeared.   \par \par \uc2 Arbitrage trade has also put pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As the Hong Kong dollar is pegged to the U.S. dollar and U.S. dollar interest rates are higher, investors make a profit on the interest rate spread by selling Hong Kong dollars for U.S. dollars.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said arbitrage trade was adding to the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's losses on Wednesday, as investors who were unwinding risky carry trades in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw Hong Kong dollar-U.S. dollar arbitrage trade as a relatively safe place to park some of their cash.   \par \par \uc2 "We're seeing interest in the Hong Kong dollar as a relatively low-risk carry trade given weakness elsewhere," said David Mann, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered Bank.   \par \par \uc2 For a story on the impact on markets of a worsening credit crunch, click on [ID:nSP16895].   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONGDOLLAR (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070801e381000uk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
