\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED-HKMA says has not  \highlight22\uc2 intervened \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market   \b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2007\par 09:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Corrects \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar rate in paragraph 4)   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, June 4 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar <HKD=>, which hit a 22-year low last month, the head of the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 HKMA chief executive Joseph Yam said in a quarterly briefing to the Legislative Council (Legco) he did not expect increasing volatility in China's exchange rate to affect the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Trade in Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has decoupled from China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year as speculation that the territory would adjust its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to let the Hong Kong dollar track the Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> has eased.   \par \par \uc2 While the yuan has been gradually appreciating, the Hong Kong dollar has weakened, hitting a 22-year low of 7.8264 on May 25.   \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85.   \par \par \uc2 The yuan's appreciation is expected to add to inflation pressure in Hong Kong, which imports much of its food from the mainland. However, K.C. Kwok, the government's chief economist, told the same Legco session that inflation remained moderate.   \par \par \uc2 He reiterated the government's forecast for a 1.5 percent increase in the composite consumer price index this year and economic growth of between 4.5 and 5.5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 During the session, Hong Kong officials again expressed concern about China's overheating stock markets but said they were confident the impact on Hong Kong's market would be limited because most participants here are professional, not retail investors. Financial Secretary Henry Tang said Hong Kong was discussing with mainland officials ways to provide a hedging mechanism to curb a widening differential in share prices traded in the two markets.   \par \par \uc2 He said possible options included a hedging mechanism through the Qualified Domestic Institutional Investor scheme, which allows banks to invest mainland investors' money in Hong Kong.   \par \par \uc2 A number of mainland Chinese companies have A shares in China and H shares in Hong Kong.   \par \par \uc2 Many A shares trade at nearly double the price of their corresponding H shares, as excess liquidity in the China market and a surge in market participation by retail investors have sent share prices soaring.   \par \par \uc2 HONGKONG-YAM (CORRECTED)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070604e364000dd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
