\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ UPDATE:HKMA Yam Says No Need To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  If HK$ Within Band   \b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2007\par 10:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2007, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quote from Joseph Yam, updates Hong Kong dollar spot rate.)   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chief Executive Joseph Yam said Monday there is no need for the territory''s de-facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar remains within its trading band.   \par \par \uc2 The local unit is pegged at HK$7.80 to the U.S. dollar and is allowed to trade between HK$7.75 and HK$7.85.   \par \par \uc2 Speaking at a meeting of the Legislative Council''s financial affairs panel, Yam said the Hong Kong dollar''s recent movement was "healthy."   \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar dropped to a 22-year low of HK$7.8251 to the U.S. dollar late Wednesday on carry trade-related demand for the U.S. dollar. It has since rebounded on the buoyant local equities market and was at HK$7.8056 at 0645 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 "A certain level of spread between Hong Kong-dollar and U.S.-dollar interest rates isn''t inconsistent with a credible convertibility zone. We don''t see the need for market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth the relationship between interest rates and the exchange rate for now," Yam said.   \par \par \uc2 He added that the Hong Kong dollar''s recent volatility was largely the result of large initial public offerings that temporarily boosted demand for the local unit. -By Jackie Cheung and Amy Or, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2832 2335; jackie.cheun