\par\par \b \uc2 DJ HKMA Yam: No Need To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  Within HKD Trading Band   \b0\par\par\uc2 174 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2007\par 04:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2007, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chief Executive Joseph Yam said Monday there is no need for the territory''s de-facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar spot rate remains within its trading band.   \par \par \uc2 The local unit was pegged at HK$7.80 to the U.S. dollar and is allowed to trade between HK$7.75 and HK$7.85.   \par \par \uc2 Speaking at a meeting of the Legislative Council''s Financial Affairs panel, Yam said the Hong Kong dollar''s recent movement was 'healthy.'   \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar dropped to a 22-year low of HK$7.8251 to the U.S. dollar late Wednesday on carry trade-related demand for the U.S. dollar. It has since rebounded on the buoyant local equities market and was at HK$7.8111 at 0200 GMT. -By Jackie Cheung and Amy Or, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2832 2335; jackie.cheung@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -0-    \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020070604e364001xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
