\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:HKMA Chief Exec Yam:Not Concerned About Weakening HK$   \b0\par\par\uc2 536 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2007\par 06:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from Yam and strategist, and updated Hong Kong dollar level.)   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chief Executive Joseph Yam said he isn't concerned about the fall in the Hong Kong dollar, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped to its lowest level against the U.S. dollar in 22 years Friday.   \par \par \uc2 "In fact, because we now have a convertibility zone, I wouldn't attach any particular significance to the position of the spot exchange rate within the zone," he said in his weekly Internet column posted Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar plunged to a fresh 22-year low of HK$7.8263 against the U.S. dollar in early morning trading Friday on carry trade-related demand for the U.S. dollar. Investors see the Hong Kong dollar as a low-risk funding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for carry trade as the Hong Kong-U.S. interest rate differential remains wide.   \par \par \uc2 The local unit was at HK$7.8242 at 0400 GMT Friday and is poised to trend lower as U.S. dollar demand persists, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 Standard Chartered PLC\uc2  strategist David Mann said he expects the local unit to test the Hong Kong dollar's weak-side border at HK$7.85 in the next two to three months, as there is no large-scale fundraising activity to offset U.S. dollar demand for carry trade.   \par \par \uc2 In his column, however, the head of the city's de-facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned of dangers related to any sudden narrowing of the U.S.-Hong Kong rate gap.   \par \par \uc2 "If the gap closes abruptly, then firms and households and the financial system in Hong Kong might suffer from a large interest-rate shock, which is not good for financial stability," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Yam said the refinements to the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peg to the U.S. dollar that were introduced two years ago have worked well so far and reiterated that there is no intention to use the Chinese yuan as the Hong Kong dollar's anchor \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 But Yam said it remains to be seen how the Hong Kong dollar will behave when it moves closer to the weak-side border at HK$7.85.   \par \par \uc2 He said \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's de-facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  only once within the HK$7.75 to HK$7.85 trading band to smooth out IPO-related interest-rate volatility.   \par \par \uc2 The HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  a week after it introduced refinement measures to the peg system on May 18, 2005 by selling HK$544 million of Hong Kong dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to address strong market demands for the local unit ahead of a slew of initial public offerings.   \par \par \uc2 In June 2005,  \uc2 Bank of Communications Ltd.\uc2  and China Cosco Holdings Ltd. raised more than US$3 billion from two large offerings.   \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged to the U.S. dollar at HK$7.80, but its trading band was widened to five Hong Kong cents below and above the peg rate on May 18, 2005 to increase the system's flexibility.   \par \par \uc2 -By Amy Or, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2832 2335; amy.or@dowjones.com [ 25-05-07 0440GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070525e35p0004l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
