\par\par \b \uc2 = WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Split Awaiting ECB, BOE Decisions-2  \b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2007\par 22:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 Feb 07, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 In Asia, the Chinese yuan blew past one end of the Hong Kong dollar's trading band with the U.S. dollar Wednesday, becoming the stronger of the two Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  without any impact on Hong Kong's two-decade-old peg to the U.S. dollar. The rate of appreciation in the yuan has accelerated in recent weeks, while the Hong Kong dollar has defied speculation it would follow the yuan and break out of its permitted trading range of HK$7.75 to HK$7.85 to the U.S. dollar. The yuan's movements versus the dollar have remained within that band since Nov. 27, and rose above the Hong Kong dollar's peg rate to the U.S. dollar Jan. 11.  \par \par \uc2 In intraday trading in Shanghai, the U.S. dollar went as low as CNY7.747, marking its lowest level since the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was revalued July 21, 2005, and sliding from Tuesday's close of CNY7.7555.  \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar, meanwhile, fell against the U.S. dollar. In Hong Kong Wednesday, the U.S. dollar rose to HK$7.8122 from HK$7.8083 late Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan began to approach parity with the Hong Kong dollar late last year, and that led many to buy the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on speculation it would keep rising in tandem with the yuan and break out of its peg system. The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it wouldn't change the peg and that it wasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's value.  \par \par \uc2 (Alastair Stewart in San Paulo, Siobhain Ryan in Shanghai and Amy Or in Hong Kong contributed to this report.)  \par \par \uc2 -By Isabelle Lindenmayer, Dow Jones Newswires, 201-938-5063; Isabelle.Lindenmayer@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 02-07-07 1635ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070207e327002lv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
