\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong dollar stays weak on corporate USD demand  \b0\par\par\uc2 527 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2007\par 11:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Jan 24 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar drifted lower on Wednesday amid commercial demand for the U.S. dollar and renewed arbitrage trades.  \par \par \uc2 The domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> was trading at 7.8029/30 to the U.S. dollar at 1000 GMT, down from 7.7988/92 in late Asia trade on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "We've seen good two-way business. There was demand for the U.S. dollar from some corporations, but some selling interest from banks when the spot rate traded at a higher level," one dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The USD/HKD spot rate is expected to move in a range between 7.7970 and 7.8050 in the near term, given that positive sentiment in the stock market may attract fund flows, but the wide interest rate differential between Hong Kong and the United States will encourage players into arbitrage, the dealer added.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark Hang Seng Index <.HSI> set a record for a third straight day before ending up 0.25 percent on Wednesday, while the index of Hong Kong-listed Chinese companies <.HSCE> gained 0.67 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weakened over recent weeks and hit a near 17-year low of 7.8122 last Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, despite suggestions to the contrary by investment bank UBS. For more details of the story, double click on [nHKG145966].  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong dollar forwards were rangebound on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The discount on forwards traded wider in the morning session, taking the cue from interest-rate swaps-related selling. However, short covering emerged in the afternoon, a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The discount on one-year forwards <HKD1Y=> was quoted at 870/855 pips, versus 890/870 pips earlier in the day and 870/850 pips late on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Interbank rates were steady to a tad softer. The overnight rate was quoted at 3.65/3.70 percent, while the one-month rate was trading at 3.85/3.88 percent versus the previous day's close of 3.86/3.91 percent.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                   At 1000 GMT   At 0400 GMT   At 0958 GMT\par HK$ SPOT <HKD=>      7.8029/30     7.8019/20     7.7988/92\par FORWARDS \par Three-month          -265/-260     -267/-262     -263/-258\par Six-month            -487/-482     -494/-488     -490/-485\par One-year             -870/-855     -882/-867     -870/-850\par INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par Overnight            3.65/3.70     3.65/3.70     3.65/3.70\par Three-month          3.95/3.98     3.95/4.00     3.98/4.03\par Six-month            4.08/4.10     4.04/4.09     4.11/4.13\par One-year             4.20/4.23     4.19/4.24     4.20/4.25\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on Reuters contributor page <FWEN>.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG-FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|Z|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070127e31o0008s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
