\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-HKMA says has not  \highlight22\uc2 intervened \highlight\uc2  on HK dollar  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Susan Fenton  \par \uc2 641 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2007\par 06:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Adds trader quote, details)  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 24 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to influence the local dollar, despite suggestions to the contrary by investment bank UBS.  \par \par \uc2  UBS suggested in a research report that the HKMA had a hand in the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent decline to stave off upward pressure after the Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> overtook the Hong Kong dollar <HKD=> in value this month.  \par \par \uc2  "The HKMA does not comment on individual reports," Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Thomas Chan said in an email to Reuters.  \par \par \uc2  "Following the introduction of the three refinements in May 2005, the Hong Kong dollar may move within the convertibility zone from 7.7500 to 7.8500," Chan added, referring to adjustments to the Hong Kong trading band in 2005.  \par \par \uc2  "We will continue to keep a close watch over the markets and keep our finger on the pulse of the markets. We have not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar as (HKMA chief executive) Mr Yam has already said last week."  \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar has weakened this year. In the past week it has fallen below its official peg at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar, hitting a near 17-year low at 7.8122 on Friday -- bucking expectations it would draw upward pressure after being overtaken in value by the yuan on Jan. 11.  \par \par \uc2  "Once the renminbi started to enter 'Hong Kong airspace' the Hong Kong dollar made a sudden jump, weakening to the other end of the band, and the renminbi made a sudden jump as well, strengthening past the Hong Kong dollar at a rapid clip," UBS economist Jonathan Anderson wrote in the research report, which circulated in the past few days.  \par \par \uc2  "This looks a lot like a Hong Kong dollar/renminbi 'squeeze play'," he wrote. "In other words, in order to minimise market speculation and volatility associated with the two exchange rates crossing each other, the HKMA and the People's Bank of China (PBOC) decide to speed up the process, the HKMA pushing the Hong Kong dollar weaker while the PBOC picks up the appreciation pace on the renminbi side."  \par \par \uc2  TRADERS DOUBTFUL  \par \par \uc2  Market traders attribute the Hong Kong dollar's decline to interest rate arbitrage activity and because demand for the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not as high as late last year when jumbo initial public offerings were launched on the stock exchange.  \par \par \uc2  "I don't think there has been any irregular activity in the market as the Hong Kong dollar is trading within the convertibility range," a trader at a European bank said.  \par \par \uc2  On Jan. 11, the yuan, also known as the renminbi, hit parity with the Hong Kong dollar at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar for the first time in 13 years and continues to appreciate.  \par \par \uc2  The yuan was trading at 7.7738 on Wednesday afternoon. The Hong Kong dollar, which is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar but since May 2005 can trade between 7.75 and 7.85, was trading at 7.8018.  \par \par \uc2  The Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation beyond the Hong Kong dollar exchange rate had raised speculation about whether Hong Kong would maintain its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  link with the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2  The HKMA has repeatedly stressed that it has no intention of abandoning its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg with the U.S. dollar and that parity with the yuan exchange rate would have no impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.  \par \par \uc2  Financial Secretary Henry Tang has said there is no question of linking the Hong Kong dollar with the yuan while the yuan is not a convertible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   (Additional reporting by Christina Lo)    \par \par \uc2 HONGKONG-MARKETS/HKDOLLAR (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070124e31o000cm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
