\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA's Yam: Yuan Rise Won't Have Strong Impact On HK Dlr  \b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2006\par 12:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar isn't likely to be significantly affected by the rise of the Chinese yuan, even if the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  breaches the psychologically important 7.80 level against the U.S. dollar, the head of Hong Kong's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The USD/CNY dipped below 8.00 Monday and that had "no noticeable effect on the exchange rate of the Hong Kong dollar," Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chief Executive Joseph Yam said in his weekly Internet column.  \par \par \uc2 He said he believed this would also be the case even if the yuan passes through "another psychological level of 7.80."  \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar was at 7.7539 against the U.S. dollar in late trade Thursday, while the yuan was at 8.0180.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  now combines a classical \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board with active \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a trading band from HK$7.75 to HK$7.85, around the fixed exchange rate of HK$7.80. The upper limit on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , imposed last year, has helped defuse market speculation that a possible appreciation of the Chinese yuan, also known as the renminbi, would also push the Hong Kong dollar higher.  \par \par \uc2 Yam said the Hong Kong dollar would have been "a much more popular proxy for market participants to take speculative positions on the renminbi" had the measure not been implemented.  \par \par \uc2 He added the widening of the Hong Kong dollar's trading band "served to anchor exchange rate expectation at a critical moment."  \par \par \uc2 Yam said China's current account surplus wouldn't be resolved by exchange rate appreciation alone. He said China has a good opportunity to further liberalize its capital account to allow the large pool of domestic savings to seek higher risk-adjusted rates of return overseas.  \par \par \uc2 -By Amy Or, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2832 2335; amy.or@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Sharon Buan [ 18-05-06 1053GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060518e25i000ow\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
