\par\par \b \uc2 DJ HK Dlr Mkts Late: HK Dlr At 4-Month High On Dlr Weakness  \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2006\par 11:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2006, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar rose to a four-month high Monday as a broadly weak dollar and concerns Asian central banks may refrain from keeping their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weak sparked selling of the U.S. unit, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar fell to HK$7.7514 in late trading from HK$7.7532 late Thursday and was down from the fixing level earlier Monday of HK$7.7522. Hong Kong was closed for a public holiday Friday. The Hong Kong dollar was at its strongest level since Jan. 11, when it also finished at HK$7.7514.  \par \par \uc2 Speculation that U.S. pressure is mounting on Japan and other Asian nations to let their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen to calm protectionist sentiment at home and reduce the huge U.S. trade deficit sent the U.S. dollar lower, traders said. That helped send the U.S. dollar to below JPY112.00 for the first time in seven-and-a-half months.  \par \par \uc2 Selling of the U.S. dollar for the Hong Kong dollar Monday stopped shy of triggering the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level of HK$7.7500, a rate at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells Hong Kong dollars to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg intact.  \par \par \uc2 'The pair is fairly heavy (low) but the support band will hold,' one senior trader said Monday.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. dollar/Hong Kong dollar forwards were lower on more confident expectations of the underlying future strength in the local unit, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The one-year contract was quoted at a 535-515 discount in late trade from a 482-472 discount late Thursday, reflecting expectations of a stronger Hong Kong dollar in a year's time compared with the current spot rate.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong interbank offered rates were lower, with the one-month rate easing to 3.91% from 4.02% late Thursday, as capital inflows into Hong Kong through the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market helped add more liquidity to the interbank market, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The one-month Hibor has 'been expensive in the past month' because of investors borrowing funds to buy into initial public offerings, including the coming US$7 billion Bank of China offer, one dealer said, but Monday's inflows helped offset that.  \par \par \uc2 - -  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020060508e258005mt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
