\par\par \b \uc2 HK Dlr Mkts Late: HK Dlr Nears Cap As Inflows Continue  \b0\par\par\uc2 510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2005\par 10:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar continued to rise against the U.S. dollar Wednesday, reaching a fresh high as investors continued to move funds into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy into big upcoming share sales.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was quoted at HK$7.7600 Wednesday afternoon, down from HK$7.7622 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 It was the closest the Hong Kong dollar has come to the upper end of its permitted trading range against the U.S. dollar since the new top limit of 7.75 was implemented in May. The Hong Kong dollar's previous high was 7.7611.  \par \par \uc2 Market participants say the past week's rise in the Hong Kong dollar is due to investors preparing funds to buy into some large initial public offerings on the local bourse in coming weeks, such as China Construction Bank and the Link real estate investment trust.  \par \par \uc2 The movements don't appear to be due to pure \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation, and so aren't likely to draw the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, one banker said.  \par \par \uc2 "After the HKMA issued the three refinements in May, I don't think speculators will try to push up the value of the Hong Kong dollar," said Mark Wan, vice president of treasury and markets for DBS Bank in Hong Kong.  \par \par \uc2 "If the money coming in was for speculation, I think the HKMA would do something," he said. "But I don't think they will do anything."  \par \par \uc2 U.S. dollar/Hong Kong dollar forwards were a touch lower Wednesday, but haven't moved dramatically despite the relatively large changes in the spot rate.  \par \par \uc2 The one-year contract was quoted at 138-128 points below the spot rate Wednesday, compared with a discount of 115-100 points Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong interbank offered rates were also stable, apparently a sign that the funds moving in for IPO purchases aren't boosting liquidity in the interbank market. The one-year Hibor was unchanged at 3.97%.  \par \par \uc2 Yields on Hong Kong Exchange Fund notes fell, tracking the overnight moves in U.S. Treasurys after producer price index data showed little increase in inflation despite high energy prices.  \par \par \uc2 The two-year Exchange Fund note was quoted at a yield of 3.59%, down from 3.65% Tuesday, while the yield on the 10-year bond eased to 4.07% from 4.12% previously.  \par \par \uc2 Chart Of Current Market Levels  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                             Latest           Late Tuesday \par Overnight Hibor              3.40%            3.20% \par 1-month Hibor                3.59%            3.61% \par 3-month Hibor                3.78%            3.77% \par 1-year Hibor                 3.97%            3.97% \par USD/HKD Spot                 HK$7.7600        HK$7.7622 \par 6-month USD/HKD Forward      -46 to -41       -33 to -28 \par 1-year USD/HKD Forward       -138 to -128     -115 to -100 \par EF Note 3.50% Jun 2015       4.07%            4.12% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Andrew Batson, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; andrew.batson@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Andrew Bullard [ 14-09-05 0806GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1053 4178  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050914e19e000cw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
