\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA Says Market  \highlight22\uc2 Operations \highlight\uc2  Will Target "Anomalies"  \b0\par\par\uc2 434 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2005\par 03:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Joseph Yam says the body's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will mainly be aimed at resolving persistent "anomalies" in the behavior of interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 The comments by Yam, made in his weekly Internet column, are an apparent attempt to clarify the quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's position and reassure market participants that the HKMA won't be a frequent actor in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 Last month, the HKMA adjusted the Hong Kong dollar's long-standing peg to the U.S. dollar to take the form of a trading band from HK$7.75 to HK$7.85, and said it would conduct market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  within that range at its own discretion. The HKMA had previously taken a more passive stance, buying or selling Hong Kong dollars only when it was approached by market players.  \par \par \uc2 "I can understand the anxiety of those active in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market about what our stance might be within the convertibility zone," Yam wrote in his column. "It shouldn't be difficult to understand our thinking."  \par \par \uc2 While insisting that the HKMA doesn't have a specific interest rate policy, Yam said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -board system implies that "in normal circumstances our interest rates track those of the U.S. dollar."  \par \par \uc2 While some interest rate volatility is normal when funds are moving into or out of Hong Kong, Yam said, "we would like also to avoid a situation where interest rate differentials become so large and persistent as to possibly jeopardize monetary and financial stability."  \par \par \uc2 Yam said he couldn't define the precise conditions that would prompt the HKMA to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the decision remains "a matter of judgment" that depends on circumstances.  \par \par \uc2 "It would be unreasonable to expect us to stand on the sidelines if credible evidence emerges of mounting instability in the market or conditions that prevent smooth interest rate adjustments," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA's shift to the current system was prompted by the persistent failure of Hong Kong interest rates to follow U.S. interest rates upward as market speculation about the appreciation of the Chinese yuan intensified.  \par \par \uc2 Since the previous arrangement didn't put an explicit limit on the appreciation of the Hong Kong dollar, market participants were unwilling to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and push its interest rates higher, because of the possible loss if the Hong Kong dollar were to rise sharply.  \par \par \uc2 -By Andrew Batson, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; andrew.batson@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Nick vonKlock [ 17-06-05 0130GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050617e16h00019\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
