\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar weakens as players cover short USD positions  \b0\par\par\uc2 604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2005\par 11:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, June 1 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar gave up recent gains on Wednesday, weighed down by a firmer U.S. dollar, dimming hopes of a near term Chinese yuan revaluation and a softening in short-dated money rates.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> weakened to a one-week low of 7.7845 per U.S. dollar at 0930 GMT from 7.7786/87 in late Asian trading on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "The U.S. dollar rebound and fading expectations of a yuan revaluation soon have put pressure on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That prompted some players to cover short (U.S.) dollar positions," said a dealer from a European bank.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong dollar forwards were rangebound following the movement in spot rate, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The discount on one-year forwards <HKD1Y=> was trading at 245/220 pips, versus 300/270 pips earlier and Tuesday's close of 270/250 pips.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar surged to a 7-\u189\'00\'BD month highs against the euro <EUR=> ahead of a Dutch vote late on Wednesday which is expected to reject the European Union constitution, after France voted against it last weekend.  \par \par \uc2 Some traders said a raging dispute between China, United States and Europe over Chinese textile exports had reduced chances of an imminent adjustment of the Chinese yuan.  \par \par \uc2 Short-term interbank rates surrendered some of their recent gains as traders worried about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA), the city's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The HKMA stands ready to provide support if coming IPOs create pressure on the money markets," HKMA chief Joseph Yam told reporters on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Interbank rates have risen in recent weeks as expected demand for IPOs put a squeeze on banks' funds.  \par \par \uc2 A spate of Chinese companies are hoping to raise about HK$60 billion from initial offering in Hong Kong in June and July.  \par \par \uc2 The mainland's largest coal producer, China Shenhua Energy Co., which plans to raise up to US$3.6 billion, will kick off its retail offering this Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "Since three IPOs will be launched one after another and not overlap each other, we don't think it will put too much (upside) pressure on the money rates if banks make appropriate arrangements beforehand," one trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight rate was quoted at 2.62-2.75 percent late on Wednesday. The two-week eased to 3.40-3.45 percent from 3.50-3.56 percent on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 However, other rates rebounded slightly from morning's low. The one-month rate was quoted at 3.43-3.46 percent versus 3.37-3.40 percent earlier but still softer than 3.43-3.48 percent in the previous close.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                 Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                 At 0930 GMT   At 0250 GMT   At 0856 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>   7.7842/45     7.7810/12     7.7786/87\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month         -5 / +5      -10 / par      -5 / +5\par  Six-month          -70 / -55     -85 / -75     -70 / -65\par  One-year          -245 / -220   -290 / -260   -270 / -250\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         2.62 / 2.75   2.80 / 2.85   2.70 / 2.75\par  Three-month       3.33 / 3.35   3.30 / 3.32   3.33 / 3.36\par  Six-month         3.33 / 3.35   3.30 / 3.32   3.31 / 3.36\par  One-year          3.43 / 3.45   3.38 / 3.43   3.40 / 3.45\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on Reuters contributor page <FWEN>.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG-FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|Z|M|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050601e161000qw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
