\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar edges lower in thin trade  \b0\par\par\uc2 628 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2005\par 11:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, May 30 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar edged lower on Monday in thin trade but dealers say the underlying tone is firm on hopes of more fund flows into the city for a string of upcoming initial public offerings (IPOs).  \par \par \uc2 "There was some U.S. dollar buying in late trade from a U.S. name, however, overall trading volume for the day was thin given the London and U.S. markets are closed for a holiday," one senior trader from a local bank said.  \par \par \uc2 The trader said he expected the spot rate to move in a range between HK$7.7750, the level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, and HK$7.7830 which should attract some (U.S.) dollar selling for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for upcoming IPOs.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Wednesday and sold HK$544 million of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exchange for U.S. dollars in a bid to curb the Hong Kong dollar's advance against the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 On May 18, the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) set a trading band for the Hong Kong dollar of between 7.75 and 7.85 to the U.S. dollar. The lower limit of the trading band will be phased in over five weeks, moving by 100 pips every Monday from May 23 until June 20. The authority also said it may conduct market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  within the "convertibility zone".  \par \par \uc2 Several IPOs by major Chinese companies worth about HK$60 billion are expected to list on the Hong Kong bourse in June and July, attracting foreign investment flows to the city.  \par \par \uc2 China Cosco Holdings Co. Ltd., which operates the world's seventh largest container fleet, began marketing a US$1.7 billion IPO on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The mainland's largest coal producer China Shenhua Energy Co., which plans to raise up to US$3.6 billion, will kick off its retail offering this Thursday. The deal is set to price on June 8 and will debut on June 15.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> was trading at 7.7797/98 per U.S. dollar at 0902 GMT after hitting an intraday's low of 7.78, weaker than 7.7968/70 in late Asian trade on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong dollar forwards were trapped in narrow ranges in quiet trade, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The discount on one-year forwards <HKD1Y=> was trading at 290/260 pips, compared with Friday's close of 310/280 pips.  \par \par \uc2 In the cash market, short-term interbank rates firmed slightly in afternoon trade with the two-week and one-month rates trading at 3.35-3.40 percent and 3.35-3.45 percent, respectively.  \par \par \uc2 Other interbank rates were little changed.  \par \par \uc2 "The large-scale IPOs should keep liquidity tight in the interbank market over the next two months," one dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                 Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                 At 0835 GMT   At 0254 GMT   At 0845 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>   7.7798/99     7.7780/84     7.7768/70\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month         -7 / +3      -13 / -3        -7 / +3\par  Six-month          -90 / -70    -100 / -80      -95 / -75\par  One-year          -290 / -260   -300 / -270    -310 / -280\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         2.70 / 2.90   2.75 / 2.75    2.70 / 2.80\par  Three-month       3.28 / 3.33   3.28 / 3.30    3.25 / 3.30\par  Six-month         3.25 / 3.35   3.28 / 3.30    3.25 / 3.30\par  One-year          3.38 / 3.43   3.35 / 3.40    3.35 / 3.40\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f