\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar firms as funds flow in for IPOs  \b0\par\par\uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 2005\par 11:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, May 27 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar edged higher on Friday, bolstered by persistent fund flows into the territory ahead of a series of China-themed initial public offerings over the next two months.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> rose to as high as 7.7765 per U.S. dollar before slipping back to 7.7768/70 by 0856 GMT, firmer than 7.7795/96 in late Asian trade on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Several initial public offerings (IPOs) by major Chinese companies worth about HK$60 billion are expected to list on the Hong Kong bourse in June and July, attracting foreign investment flows to the territory.  \par \par \uc2 At the head of the IPO queue is the top mainland coal producer China Shenhua Energy Co., which plans to raise up to US$3.6 billion next week. The deal is set to price on June 8 and will debut on June 15.  \par \par \uc2 Interbank rates softened from recent highs amid a firming local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as some banks were willing to release excess funds, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Some traders also attributed the decline to players adjusting positions on concern about further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA).  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA, the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday and sold HK$544 million of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exchange for U.S. dollar in a bid to curb the Hong Kong dollar's advance against the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 Interbank rates rose last week as liquidity tightened following HKMA moves to refine the exchange rate system, and as players positioned themselves for the upcoming IPOs in the stock market. Some investors withdrew funds from the territory after the HKMA announced its new measures.  \par \par \uc2 On May 18, the HKMA set a trading band for the Hong Kong dollar (HKD) of between 7.75 and 7.85 to the U.S. dollar in a move to prop up interest rates and discourge speculators using the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bet on a revaluation of the Chinese yuan.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight interbank rate eased to 2.70-2.80 percent late on Friday versus a recent high of 3.25 percent. The three-month rate was around 3.23-3.35 percent, down from 3.35-3.40 percent in the previous day.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong dollar forwards eased on Friday on the back of a softening in short-dated money rates.  \par \par \uc2 The discount on one-year forwards <HKD1Y=> widened to 310/280 pips from Thursday's close of 250/220 pips.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                 Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                 At 0845 GMT   At 0330 GMT   At 0858 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>   7.7768/70     7.7792/93     7.7795/96\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month         -7 / - 3      -3 / +7      + 7 / +17\par  Six-month          -95 / -75     -80 / -60     -70 / -50\par  One-year          -310 / -280   -285 / -255   -250 / -220\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         2.70 / 2.80   2.75 / 2.75   2.50 / 2.75\par  Three-month       3.25 / 3.30   3.25 / 3.30   3.35 / 3.40\par  Six-month         3.25 / 3.30   3.25 / 3.30   3.30 / 3.40\par  One-year          3.35 / 3.40   3.35 / 3.40   3.35 / 3.45\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on Reuters contributor page <FWEN>.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG-FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|Z|M|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050527e15r000xh\par }\page {\pa