\par\par \b \uc2 DJ HK Dlr Mkts Late: Hibors Up On HKD Demand Ahead Of IPOs-2-  \b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 2005\par 11:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Hong Kong interbank offered rates rose further Thursday, boosted by increased demand for the local dollar ahead of several initial public offerings in coming months.  \par \par \uc2 The one-month Hibor was last quoted at 3.43%, up from 3.20% Wednesday, while the one-year Hibor rose to 3.47% from 3.35%.  \par \par \uc2 'Demand for the Hong Kong dollar has already risen on worries of inadequate liquidity once the subscription process begins for IPOs,' said a trader at a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 He said he expects short-dated Hibors to remain high in the near term due to the buoyant demand, but said the demand is only temporary.  \par \par \uc2 'Rates will likely ease slightly for several weeks after the completion of the IPOs,' he said.  \par \par \uc2 Among major IPOs in the next two months are those of coal producer Shenhua Energy Co., China's Bank of Communications, and COSCO Holdings Ltd., China's largest shipping firm.  \par \par \uc2 The companies are expected to raise more than HK$50 billion in total from their offerings.  \par \par \uc2 But the trader said the decline in Hibors should be limited after the share offerings. He said local rates will continue to correspond to U.S. rates after the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced last week a ceiling to the local dollar's exchange rate to the U.S. dollar to discourage its use as a trading proxy for the yuan.  \par \par \uc2 On the spot market, the Hong Kong dollar weakened slightly against the U.S. dollar, after the HKMA sold HK$544 million worth of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday to buy U.S. dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was last quoted at HK$7.7799, up slightly from HK$7.7795 previously.  \par \par \uc2 The trader said Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 'just the beginning.'  \par \par \uc2 'With increasing demand for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar and continued yuan speculation, the HKMA may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again once the local dollar rises to HK$7.775 against the U.S. dollar,' he said.  \par \par \uc2 He said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also necessary to prevent Hibors from rising too quickly.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. dollar/Hong Kong dollar forwards rose, mainly on profit-taking after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 'Players are taking profit as they don't expect the local dollar to be allowed to appreciate much in the near term,' the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The one-year U.S. dollar/Hong Kong dollar forward was quoted at 250-230 points below the spot rate, narrowing from 320-305 points Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Yields on Exchange Fund notes fell slightly, despite stronger demand for local dollar-denominated assets.  \par \par \uc2 The 10-year note was quoted at 3.64%, compared with 3.67% previously. Chart Of Current Market Levels  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Latest          Late Wednesday \par Overnight Hibor              3.16%           2.90% \par 1-month Hibor                3.43%           3.20% \par 3-month Hibor                3.42%           3.25% \par 1-year Hibor                 3.47%           3.35% \par USD/HKD Spot                 HK$7.7799       HK$7.7795 \par 6-month USD/HKD Forward      -68 to -58      -105 to -90 \par 1-year USD/HKD Forward       -250 to -230    -320 to -305 \par EF Note 3.51% Dec 2014       3.64%           3.67% \par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Jeffrey Ng, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; jeffrey.ng@dowjones.com -Edited by Andrew Bullard -0-   \f28 \pa