\par\par \b \uc2 HK interbank rates remain firm on IPO-related fund demand  \b0\par\par\uc2 481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 2005\par 05:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, May 26 (Reuters) - Hong Kong interbank rates remained firm on Thursday morning on persistent demand for funds ahead of several large China share offerings next month.  \par \par \uc2 The overnight rate was quoted at 3.10-3.15 percent, while the one-month to six-month rates rose to 3.35-3.40 percent from 3.20-3.30 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Market liquidity has tightened since last week after some outflow of funds from the banking system and as players position themselves for a series of upcoming initial public offerings (IPOs) in the stock market.  \par \par \uc2 China IPO's worth HK$50 billion are expected to list on the Hong Kong bourse in June and July including China Shenhua Energy Co., Bank of Communications and China's COSCO Holdings.  \par \par \uc2 Some traders said the tightness in liquidity was partly due to the uneven distribution of funds among banks. Short-term liquidity is controlled by just a handful of major banks.  \par \par \uc2 In the spot market, the Hong Kong dollar was steady after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday afternoon to stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advance against the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> shuffled between 7.7780 and 7.7805 during the session. It was trading at 7.7798/7.7805 at 0310 GMT versus 7.7820/22 in late Asian trading on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The three-month Hong Kong dollar forwards rose to the premium level from a discount on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 A dealer from a European bank said the overnight to three-month forwards have risen to a premium level from a discount in recent sessions due to the fact local interbank rates were slightly higher than U.S. dollar LIBOR amid tighter liquidity.  \par \par \uc2 The discount on one-year forwards <HKD1Y=> narrowed to 250/230 pips from Wednesday's close of 310/280 pips.  \par \par \uc2 "I expect the forwards to remain range trading. Short-term liquidity is likely to remain tight in the run-up of the IPOs, so the one-year forwards are expected to move between -200 and -350 pips," one dealer at a local bank said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                 Morning       Previous Close\par                 At 0310 GMT   At 0940 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>   7.7798/7.7805 7.7820/22\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month        + 5 / +15     -7 / +2\par  Six-month          -65 / -45    -100 / -85\par  One-year          -250 / -230   -310 / -280\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         3.10 / 3.15   3.00 / 3.12\par  Three-month       3.35 / 3.40   3.18 / 3.33\par  Six-month         3.35 / 3.40   3.17 / 3.32\par  One-year          3.40 / 3.45   3.22 / 3.37\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on Reuters contributor page <FWEN>.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG-FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|Z|M|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050526e15q000b1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
