\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar trims early gains after HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 693 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2005\par 12:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , May 25 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar trimmed some of its early gains on Wednesday after the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) stepped into the market in the afternoon to stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advance against the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <HKD=> was trading at 7.7820/22 per U.S. dollar at 0940 GMT after hitting a five-month high of 7.7750, and weaker than 7.7803/05 in late Asian trading on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA, the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sold HK$544 million of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exchange for U.S. dollars. This is the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the HKMA since it set an upper limit for the HKD/USD trading band last week and is the first time since Dec. 10, 2004 that the HKMA has sold Hong Kong dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The move by the HKMA will lift the aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- to HK$1.317 billion after settlement on Friday, compared with HK$726 million on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Last Wednesday, the HKMA set a trading band for the Hong Kong dollar of between 7.75 and 7.85 to the U.S. dollar. The lower limit for the Hong Kong dollar will move 100 pips every Monday, starting with a move to 7.81 on May 23, until it reaches 7.85 by June 20.  \par \par \uc2 After the announcement of the trading band by the HKMA, there was some HK$3.12 billion in fund outflows from the banking system as players closed their long Hong Kong dollar positions.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong interbank rates spiked higher after the sudden reduction in liquidity, spurring banks to raise their prime and saving deposit rates by 50 basis points on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The market has also been short of liquidity after a fall in the aggregate balance last week, with some players selling U.S. dollars for the Hong Kong dollars in recent days, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "The U.S. dollar selling (by the banks) has sparked the HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer from a European bank.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank rates softened slightly after the HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The overnight rate was quoted at 3.00-3.12 percent versus 3.06-3.18 percent the previous day.  \par \par \uc2 Discounts on longer-dated \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar forwards widened initially after the HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but then narrowed.  \par \par \uc2 "Since market liquidity was still tight with the overnight interbank rate sustained over 3 percent, the downside for forwards would be limited," another trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The discount on one-year forwards <HKD1Y=> was at 310/280 pips versus Tuesday's close of 350/330 pips.  \par \par \uc2 There was also talk in the market that the tightening in liquidity was due to strong demand for funds ahead of China-themed initial public offerings (IPOs) in the territory.  \par \par \uc2 "Banks are preparing funding ahead of a number of big IPOs in June," said a dealer from a European bank.  \par \par \uc2 Prospective IPOs in June include China Shenhua Energy Co., which plans to raise US$3 billion, Bank of Communications, which aims to launch US$1.5 billion, and China's COSCO Holdings, which could raise up to US$1-2 billion.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                 Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                 At 0940 GMT   At 0244 GMT   At 0904 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT <HKD=>   7.7820/22     7.7770/72     7.7803/05\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month         -7 / +2      par / +10     -25 / -15\par  Six-month         -100 / -85     -95 / -75    -135 / -115\par  One-year          -310 / -280   -300 / -280   -350 / -330\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         3.00 / 3.12   3.10 / 3.20   3.06 / 3.12\par  Three-month       3.18 / 3.33   3.25 / 3.31   3.12 / 3.17\par  Six-month         3.17 / 3.32   3.25 / 3.31   3.17 / 3.22\par  One-year          3.22 / 3.37   3.31 / 3.43   3.30 / 3.35\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on Reuters contributor page <FWEN>.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG-FORWARDS|LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|Z|M|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050525e15p000y5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
