\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED-HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to support HK dollar, buys HK$3.12 bln  \b0\par\par\uc2 181 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2005\par 13:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  story, "HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support HK dollar, buys HK$3.12 bln," please read in second paragraph "...1100 GMT..." instead of "...0900 GMT..." (this corrects time).  \par \par \uc2 A corrected repetition follows.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, May 18 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA), the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said on Wednesday that it bought HK$3.12 billion ($400.1 million) banks in exchange for U.S. dollars to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 A Reuters page <HKMAOOC> showed the transaction occurred at 1100 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The move came after the HKMA announced it was introducing a trading band for the Hong Kong dollar which it hopes will reduce speculation in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the HKMA will reduce the aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- to HK$714 million after settlement on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HONGKONG-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CORRECTED)|LANGEN|ABN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|Z|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050518e15i0015c\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \ce